,'2024-09-23 02:45:15','2024-09-23 02:45:15'),(11325,'judge-event-evaluation-14613-1727023569',14613,119,7,7,2,2024,350,'718','1',0,392,6960,31,NULL,NULL,100,77.00,NULL,NULL,'Great work Artia, a great start into Instrumental arranging. Amazing grace is a really good base to work with as well, there is so much you can do with it.\r\nI\'d love to see more work with modulating/transitioning chords, and just some work on making it flow - perhaps the first verse could have been more traditional, as opposed to heavy chords.\r\nOverall, great work, keep it up. Please also make sure that you supply all the paperwork. God bless!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-09-23 02:46:09','2024-09-23 02:46:09'),(11326,'judge-event-evaluation-18261-1727023613',18261,226,7,7,2,2024,364,'760','1',0,7991,8451,26,'Open','21',100,89.00,-10,NULL,'Better choose praise song.\r\nKeep dancing for Jesus!!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-09-23 02:46:53','2024-09-23 02:46:53'),(11327,'judge-event-evaluation-9885-1727023716',9885,237,7,7,2,2024,198,'510',NULL,8080,5934,7373,53,'Collection',NULL,100,84.00,-10,NULL,'Allegra finished her art nicely.\r\nYet, the judge can find a combined shape looks like a puppy in the house.\r\nIt can be a good title for the art.\r\nWell done, Allegra!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-09-23 02:48:36','2024-09-23 02:48:36'),(11328,'judge-event-evaluation-14591-1727024149',14591,119,7,7,2,2024,348,'768','1',0,392,6960,31,NULL,NULL,100,82.00,NULL,NULL,'Great work Mazmur, a great base to work with - it has some already nice transitioning chords, and is a simple yet beautiful piece.\r\nThere are some notation issues - mostly with quavers. They should never be joined over the middle of a bar, and some aren\'t joined either. Also, you can\'t use crotchet quaver crotchet quaver quaver quaver in 4/4 timing - you would need to split the middle crotchet into two stand alone quavers and tie them.\r\nAlso, it would be good to work on your cadences. Have some dissonant chords that resolve, rather than just hitting the final note.\r\nLastly, there are times when it would be good to have different instruments quieter than others - i like that you did add dynamics - sometimes it was a bit of a noisy muddle.\r\n\r\nOverall, great work, keep it up. God bless!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-09-23 02:55:49','2024-09-23 02:55:49'),(11329,'judge-event-evaluation-18461-1727025036',18461,104,7,7,2,2024,198,'510',NULL,7492,394,7373,53,'Collection',NULL,100,86.00,-10,NULL,'Jewel finished a great art.\r\nYet, he needs to provide the description and the original picture.\r\nGreat work, Jewel!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-09-23 03:10:36','2024-09-23 03:10:36'),(11330,'judge-event-evaluation-16148-1727025240',16148,263,7,7,2,2024,198,'510',NULL,8267,6328,7373,53,'Collection',NULL,100,80.00,-10,NULL,'Aaron has a great idea depicting in his art. \r\nWell done, Aaron!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-09-23 03:14:00','2024-09-23 03:14:01'),(11331,'judge-event-evaluation-8830-1727025683',8830,232,7,7,2,2024,198,'510',NULL,7047,4679,7373,53,'Collection',NULL,100,94.00,-10,