,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-06-30 17:47:13','2025-06-30 17:47:13'),(15192,'judge-event-evaluation-21386-1751276379',21386,344,16,11,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7659,55,7888,6,'Collection',NULL,100,78.00,-10,NULL,'I really  love this poem. I was just a bit confused because the title was, my friends at school, but the first paragraph wasn\'t about the friends, but how you feel when you arrive at school. Until I read the second paragraph, I didn\'t understand how the title related. Next time I suggest a title that makes sense about the whole poem. Other than that your poem was terrific, you had excellent grammar, I loved how you rhymed and how it felt like I was there in person. Keep up the good work, and hopefully we will see you next year again, to submit another wonderful poem!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-06-30 19:39:39','2025-06-30 19:39:39'),(15195,'judge-event-evaluation-21731-1751278373',21731,344,16,11,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,8847,55,7888,6,'Collection',NULL,100,80.00,-10,NULL,'Your poem is well written. It all consistently rhymes except for this one part. I\'m not sure if that was intended or not.\r\n\r\nThe sun shines equally on evil and good\r\nThe Lord is kind to every mankind\r\n\r\nAlso for this line, if you want consistent syllables, you may want to get rid of one.\r\n\r\nHold your anger, don’t let it on.\r\n\r\nA good piece of advice, I\'m not sure if you did this, is read the whole poem to yourself aloud before submitting. Then you can hear the places where there is too many syllables, or when things do not rhyme.\r\n\r\nThings I loved about your poem:\r\n\r\nHas a clear and spiritually meaningful theme\r\n\r\nUses poetic techniques like rhyme and parallelism\r\n\r\nProvides emotional and biblical depth\r\n\r\nCommunicates its message with clarity and grace\r\n\r\nThank you so much for your effort, Joren, you did a great job, and we can\'t wait to see you at accelerate conventions next year!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-06-30 20:12:53','2025-06-30 20:12:53'),(15196,'judge-event-evaluation-21393-1751279461',21393,344,16,11,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,7675,55,7888,7,'Collection',NULL,100,80.00,-10,NULL,'You put so much effort into this story and the book was amazing.\r\n\r\nThings I loved about your story was -\r\n\r\nClear Story Arc – The story has a beginning (conflict: accidental submission), middle (training, self-doubt, small victories), and end (success + emotional closure).\r\n\r\nTheme & Message – Perseverance, faith, and unexpected personal growth come through clearly.\r\n\r\nRelatable Protagonist – Amelia’s nervousness and internal thoughts are believable and make her sympathetic.\r\n\r\nUplifting Ending – The victory and surprise award are emotionally satisfying.\r\n\r\nThings that need improving-\r\n\r\nGrammar / Minor Issues\r\n“People were sitting in their classrooms” – a little clunky; maybe “students had returned to their classrooms.”\r\n\r\n“Some people roared for their school, some people cheered and clapped” – you can trim this repetition for rhythm.\r\n\r\nWatch tense shifts: The story is mostly past tense but occasionally drifts into present (e.g., \"Currently, Amelia is playing badminton\").\r\n\r\nBuild Tension Through Structure & Pacing\r\nbecause the story is too fast in the most important bits- the race- the bit you want to prolong. It misses the tension and anticipation of a big sports moment.\r\n\r\nYou did a well done, and I say you are very talented, I saw your poetry, and think you are talented. Keep up the good work, and maybe one day you will even be writing as an author!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-06-30 20:31:01','2025-06-30 20:31:01'),(15198,'judge-event-evaluation-22031-1751280350',22031,344,16,11,3,2025,272,'855',NULL,8882,55,7240,33,'Open','25',100,66.00,-10,NULL,'Time 3:59 Thank you Lydia for your song. A Helpful tip try to sing the same way the sheet music is written,(verses, chorus, order). Also practicing on hitting the notes at their exact tune to get the best sound from your singing. All in all keep practicing the gifting God has given you.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-06-30 20:45:50','2025-06-30 20:45:50'),(15199,'judge-times-event-evaluation-19646-1751319509',19646,347,16,11,3,2025,27,'104',NULL,8769,5806,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'07:37:00.830',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 07:38:29',NULL),(15200,'judge-times-event-evaluation-19664-1751319542',19664,347,16,11,3,2025,71,'204',NULL,7813,5806,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'07:25:00.020',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 07:39:02',NULL),(15201,'judge-times-event-evaluation-20528-1751319611',20528,344,16,11,3,2025,39,'134',NULL,7659,55,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'07:31:00.900',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 07:40:11',NULL),(15202,'judge-times-event-evaluation-20783-1751319637',20783,344,16,11,3,2025,53,'164',NULL,7696,55,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'07:20:00.000',NULL,NULL