5,'Collection','25',100,94.00,-10,NULL,'Great effort in coming forward to present — well done! However, there\'s room for improvement in both memorization and voice projection. Strengthening your recall will help you stay more connected to the performance, and projecting your voice will ensure the audience can fully appreciate your expression.\r\n\r\nVinaka',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 19:18:29','2025-07-01 19:18:29'),(15786,'judge-event-evaluation-22154-1751361839',22154,344,16,11,3,2025,300,'924',NULL,7721,55,7756,45,'Collection','25',100,95.00,-10,NULL,'Great performance and commendable confidence in coming forward! You used gestures well, though try to maintain them throughout. Focus on projecting your voice more and speak from the heart — with practice, your confidence and impact will grow even stronger. Keep it up!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 19:23:59','2025-07-01 19:23:59'),(15787,'judge-event-evaluation-20612-1751361993',20612,345,16,11,3,2025,300,'924',NULL,7519,5804,7756,45,'Collection','25',100,91.00,-10,NULL,'Great performance and commendable confidence in coming forward! You used gestures well, though try to maintain them throughout. Focus on projecting your voice more and speak from the heart — with practice, your confidence and impact will grow even stronger. Keep it up!\r\n\r\nVinaka.\r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 19:26:33','2025-07-01 19:26:33'),(15788,'judge-event-evaluation-22007-1751362370',22007,344,16,11,3,2025,300,'924',NULL,7679,55,7756,45,'Collection','25',100,97.00,-10,NULL,'Great performance, Tiare! You delivered with confidence, which was wonderful to see. Just remember that your approach and departure are part of the overall presentation, and try to incorporate more gestures to enhance your expression. Well done!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 19:32:50','2025-07-01 19:32:50'),(15789,'judge-event-evaluation-21890-1751362481',21890,344,16,11,3,2025,300,'924',NULL,8816,55,7756,45,'Collection','25',100,85.00,-10,NULL,'Well done on having the courage to present — that’s an achievement in itself! With more practice, smoother delivery, clear voice, expressive gestures, and eye contact, your recitation will grow even stronger. Keep it up!\r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 19:34:41','2025-07-01 19:34:41'),(15790,'judge-event-evaluation-22004-1751362533',22004,344,16,11,3,2025,300,'924',NULL,7676,55,7756,45,'Collection','25',100,100.00,-10,NULL,'Well done, Jessira Yee! Your time was 1:14.42 mins.\r\nYou delivered an excellent performance. Your fluency was outstanding — loud, clear, and spoken with confidence. Keep it up.\r\n\r\nBlessings.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 19:35:33','2025-07-01 19:35:33'),(15792,'judge-event-evaluation-22005-1751362808',22005,344,16,11,3,2025,300,'924',NULL,8850,55,7756,45,'Collection','25',100,90.00,-10,NULL,'Great performance and commendable confidence in coming forward! You used gestures well, though try to maintain them throughout. Focus on projecting your voice more and speak from the heart — with practice, your confidence and impact will grow even stronger. Keep it up!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 19:40:08','2025-07-01 19:40:08'),(15793,'judge-event-evaluation-21892-1751362831',21892,344,16,11,3,2025,300,'924',NULL,8822,55,7756,45,'Collection','25',100,95.00,-10,-0.50,'Speech well delivered. Sainimere, needs to improve on her time, as her time was -34.72secs.\r\n\r\nVinaka',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 19:40:31','2025-07-01 19:40:31'),(15795,'judge-event-evaluation-20993-1751366781',20993,344,16,11,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,8815,55,7888,6,'Collection',NULL,100,75.00,-10,NULL,'First of all, great job at this poem you did well. First Ill give you some advice, and then Ill tell you what I liked about the poem.\r\n\r\n1. Rhyming Pattern\r\nThe poem mostly tries to rhyme, which is great! But in some places, the rhymes don’t quite match or feel a little forced.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\"With just a rock—he wasn’t lying!\"\r\n\r\n“Lying” doesn\'t rhyme very well with “giant” from the line before. It feels like it’s trying to rhyme, but it doesn’t quite work.\r\n\r\nFix idea: Try ending the line with a word that sounds more like \"giant\" or change the last word of the first line to match a new rhyme.\r\n\r\n2. Rhythm (how the poem sounds when read out loud)\r\nSome lines have more words or syllables than others, which makes the rhythm feel a little bumpy.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\"And made a lunch feed quite a few.\"\r\n\r\nThis line feels a little awkward to read. It sounds rushed and doesn’t flow as smoothly.\r\n\r\nFix idea: Try something smoother like:\r\n\r\n\"He made one lunch feed quite a crowd.\"\r\nThis keeps the meaning but sounds better when spoken.\r\n\r\n3. Small grammar things\r\nExample:\r\n\"And guess what? He always cared!\"\r\n\r\n\"Cared\" is past tense, but the poem is mostly in present tense (like \"loves\" and \"helps\"). It’s better to keep the tense the same all the way through.\r\n\r\nFix idea: Change \"cared\" to \"cares\" so it matches the rest:\r\n\r\n\"And guess what? He always cares!\"\r\n\r\n4. Dashes and punctuation\r\nExample:\r\n\"With just a rock-he wasn’t lying!\"\r\n\r\nThat dash (“-”) should have a space before and after it to be easier to read:\r\n\r\n\"With just a rock – he wasn’t lying!\"\r\n\r\nOr you could even use a comma if you want it to be a softer pause.\r\n\r\nWhat I especially loved about your poem was:\r\n\r\n1. Great Message\r\n\r\nYour poem talks about God’s love, power, and care, which is a really nice and comforting message. You remind people that:\r\n\r\nGod made amazing things (like stars and the sea),\r\nHe helps people (like David),\r\nJesus did miracles (like walking on water),\r\nAnd God still loves us and helps us today.\r\n\r\n That’s powerful and kind — great job!\r\n\r\n 2. Rhyming!\r\nYou used rhymes in your poem, which makes it fun to read and helps it sound musical.\r\n\r\nExamples:\r\n\r\n“Sea” and “me” rhyme.\r\n\r\n“Bad” and “sad” rhyme.\r\n\r\nRhyming is hard, and you did a great job with most of them.\r\n\r\n3. It Feels Personal\r\nYou wrote about your feelings—like being scared or sad—and how you talk to God. That makes the poem feel real and meaningful.\r\n\r\nWhen writing comes from the heart, people connect with it more.\r\n\r\n4. You Used Bible Stories Creatively\r\nYou included famous Bible stories, like:\r\n\r\nDavid and Goliath\r\nJesus walking on water\r\nThe miracle of the loaves and fish\r\n\r\nThat’s a smart way to show how powerful and loving God is.\r\n\r\n5. It Has a Happy, Hopeful Feeling\r\nEven when you mention being scared or sad, the poem still reminds us that God is always there.\r\n\r\n6. It’s Easy to Understand\r\nYour poem uses simple, clear words that kids and adults can both understand and that’s important because poems should speak to people, not confuse them.\r\n\r\nYou did a wonderful job, and I hope you come to do accelerates conventions again next year! God bless.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 20:46:21','2025-07-01 20:46:21'),(15796,'judge-event-evaluation-20285-1751367824',20285,346,16,11,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,8711,4208,7888,6,NULL,NULL,100,69.00,-10,NULL,'Well done on a really nice, short poem.\r\n\r\nThe first thing I noticed was that the title wasn\'t underlined,  and it seemed liked the title was apart of the poem. So this made it a bit confusing when trying to read it.\r\n\r\nI also noticed that you need to work on  using the typical formatting style.\r\nYou did formatting such as:\r\n\r\nA plant sprouts,\r\n\r\nAre we proud?\r\n\r\nA rocket is launched!\r\n\r\nWe Applaud.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThe proper format technique would be like this,\r\n\r\nA plant sprouts, \r\nAre we proud?\r\nA rocket is launched!\r\nWe applaud!\r\n\r\nLearn to differentiate,\r\nlearn to appreciate.\r\nMan made.\r\nGod made.\r\n\r\nWe tend to notice,\r\nLoudness and colorfulness,\r\nbut fail to appreciate,\r\nnature at its best.\r\n\r\nWhat I loved about your poem:\r\n\r\n1- It makes you think\r\nYour poem asks a smart question:\r\nWhy do we get so excited about rockets, but not about plants growing?\r\nThat helps people stop and think, which is a really great thing for a poem to do.\r\n\r\n2-It’s easy to understand\r\nThe words are clear and not too fancy, so kids and grown-ups can both read it and get the message.\r\n\r\n3-It has a good rhythm\r\nThe way the lines are written makes it fun to read out loud. It almost sounds like music when you say it.\r\n\r\n4-It talks about something important\r\nYou\'re reminding people to appreciate nature—like trees, flowers, and animals—not just loud or shiny things like rockets and machines. That’s a message the world needs!\r\n\r\n5-It feels calm and kind\r\nInstead of shouting or blaming anyone, the poem gently shares an idea. That makes people more likely to listen and think about it.\r\n\r\nThankyou so much for contributing to our Under 16\'s poetry category, you did a brilliant job, and I hope that next year you will come back with even more!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 21:03:44','2025-07-01 21:03:44'),(15798,'judge-event-evaluation-21730-1751370069',21730,344,16,11,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7651,55,7888,6,'Collection',NULL,100,80.00,-10,NULL,'Thankyou Eshal for creating such a stunning masterpiece on the life of Napoleon. \r\n\r\nFirst I will start on a good note and tell you what I loved about your poem the most!\r\n\r\nYou tell a clear story in chronological order, making it easy to follow Napoleon’s rise and fall.\r\n\r\nThe progression from Corsica, through revolution and war, to his deathbed shows a thoughtful structure.\r\nThe ending stanza shows an attempt to explore deeper emotions — regret, repentance, mercy — which adds a spiritual and reflective layer.\r\n\r\nThat emotional turn creates a sense of closure and gives the poem a meaningful conclusion.\r\n\r\nI only have two pieces of advice for you.\r\n1-\r\nSome lines feel a bit awkward or unclear, especially early on.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n“Not America / Which got sold / To a land of gold” — It’s not obvious what you mean here. Are you saying Corsica is not America, which was sold? Or something else? The phrasing is confusing.\r\n\r\n2-\r\n“This ways to him the best solution” is grammatically off and unclear. Possibly you meant:\r\n“This was to him the best solution” or “This seemed to him the best solution.”\r\n\r\n“He was a threat none could ignore” — This is fine but could be more vivid or active.\r\n\r\nThe phrase “with a cry for” near the end of the third stanza is incomplete; a cry for what?\r\n\r\nOther than those two things, you did a terrific job! I really hope you will come back to accelerate conventions next year in 2026!\r\n\r\nPhilippians 4:13- For I can do all things through Christ who strengthens me.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 21:41:09','2025-07-01 21:41:09'),(15799,'judge-event-evaluation-21385-1751371557',21385,344,16,11,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,8845,55,7888,6,'Collection',NULL,100,78.00,-10,NULL,'hello notes-\r\n\r\nThings that might need improving if you want:\r\n\r\nYour poem follows a loose meter but isn’t fully consistent. If you want a smoother musicality, consider keeping syllable counts more even line to line. For example:\r\n\r\nOriginal:\r\n\"Birds singing in the tree tops / As nature slowly awakes.\"\r\n\r\nSmoothed:\r\n\"Birdsong from the treetops / As nature starts to wake.\"\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat was Done Well?\r\n1. Strong, Clear Theme\r\nThe poem explores the idea of perfection in nature and creation, challenging the idea that \"nothing can be perfect.\"\r\n\r\nIt presents a hopeful, spiritual, and uplifting message, which resonates emotionally with many readers.\r\n\r\n2. Imagery and Sensory Language\r\nLines like “The sunrise in the morning”, “Birds singing in the tree tops”, and “nature slowly awakes” use vivid natural imagery that helps the reader visualize and feel the scene.\r\n\r\nThis effectively brings the reader into a calm, peaceful setting.\r\n\r\n3. Consistent Rhyme Scheme\r\nThe poem uses an ABCB rhyme scheme with some couplets (e.g., \"break\" / \"awakes\"), giving it a smooth, melodic flow.\r\n\r\nThis consistency adds a musical quality and makes it pleasant to read aloud.\r\n\r\n4. Spiritual and Reflective Tone\r\nThe closing lines bring a spiritual layer, referencing God and creation. This ties the poem’s theme to a higher purpose, adding depth.\r\n\r\nThe word “woven” especially stands out—suggesting careful, intentional craftsmanship in creation.\r\n\r\n5. Positive Perspective\r\nIt gently pushes back on cynicism (“Nothing they say can be perfect”) by showing beauty in everyday life.\r\n\r\nThat affirmative tone can be comforting or inspiring to readers.\r\n\r\nThankyou for that beautiful poem, I really hope you will enter next year in the same category again!\r\n\r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 22:05:57','2025-07-01 22:05:57'),(15800,'judge-event-evaluation-21382-1751372253',21382,344,16,11,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7671,55,7888,6,'Collection',NULL,100,82.00,-10,NULL,'Hi beautiful Florence, this work of poetry was heart filled and encouraging. Keep up the good work!\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nTo improve your poem, focus on smoothing the rhythm by reading each line aloud to catch awkward phrasing. Use vivid, poetic language—try replacing simple words with more expressive or symbolic ones. Avoid forced rhymes; choose words that both fit naturally and enhance the meaning. Lastly, aim for consistent tone and imagery to create a stronger emotional impact.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nYour poem has a sincere, heartfelt tone and a clear spiritual message, which gives it emotional depth. The use of biblical imagery (Eden, the fall, Satan) and natural beauty (flowers, streams, Alps) adds strong contrast and helps convey awe and gratitude. Your consistent rhyme scheme also gives the poem a pleasant, lyrical quality. Overall, it’s thoughtful and rooted in a meaningful theme.\r\n\r\nYou did a beautiful poem, and we, at accelerate hope you will come back to the 2026 convention.\r\n\r\nI would love to give you a bible verse. 1 Corinthians 2:9\r\nIf you have time read this verse feel free to, I love adding verses of encouragement to Gods children. I used the NLT but any bible version will do!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 22:17:33','2025-07-01 22:17:33'),(15801,'judge-event-evaluation-20581-1751373120',20581,345,16,11,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,8765,5804,7888,6,'Collection',NULL,100,78.00,-10,NULL,'For a 11  or almost 11 year old, this is a really great poem! I loved it.\r\n\r\nMy only piece of advice is that some lines have too many extra words and syllables. For instance,\r\n\r\n\"In all I do that brings glory rather than fame\" Maybe you could find a way to make the sentence shorter. As you grow older, you will learn more things like this :)\r\n\r\nWhat I loved about your poem was that it rhymed beautifully, your format was lovely, and the theme in general was just amazing, showing how your God given talent for guitar can lift God up!\r\n\r\nThankyou so much beautiful girl! Hopefully next year you can come back and do another one!\r\n\r\nHere is a bible verse for you- Philippians 4:13 (Ill give you the homework, go look it up in your bible) This is for a bit of encouragement on your journey.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 22:32:00','2025-07-01 22:32:00'),(15803,'judge-event-evaluation-21305-1751374014',21305,344,16,11,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7638,55,7888,6,'Collection',NULL,100,79.00,-10,NULL,'Great job on a fantastic poem. Thankyou for trying so hard! You did a really good job!\r\n\r\nHere\'s a few things you might want to work on for next time:\r\n\r\nUse simpler words (e.g. \"plan\" and \"parables\" might need context).\r\n\r\nBreak longer sentences into shorter ones.\r\n\r\nUse a more conversational or story-like tone.\r\n\r\nExplain big ideas in a more relatable way (e.g. \"tempted by the devil\" might become \"the devil tried to trick Him\").\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nThings I loved about the poem:\r\n\r\nClear Storyline:\r\n You told the story in a simple, straightforward way that’s easy to follow—from coming to Earth to staying true and powerful.\r\n\r\nGood Rhythm and Rhyme: \r\nYour poem mostly has a nice rhythm and rhyme scheme, which makes it fun and memorable to read.\r\n\r\nStrong Message:\r\n You focused on important ideas like truth, faith, and overcoming challenges—these are inspiring and meaningful.\r\n\r\nUse of Contrast: \r\nYou showed how He was tempted but stayed truthful, which adds depth to the story.\r\n\r\nPositive Ending: \r\nEnding with the idea that truth lasts forever leaves the reader with a hopeful feeling.\r\n\r\n\r\nSo thankyou so much Grace, you did a really good poem. I also want to remind you of how much Jesus loves you. It may get old how many times people say it, but Jesus loves you more than life itself. And you deserve to be Gods special Princess!\r\n\r\nHere is a bible verse I like to read to different students- Proverbs 28:13 I used NLT but Id love if you read it. Its a good reminder to keep reading Gods word. :)\r\n\r\nThankyou so much, Grace, and we can\'t wait to see you at the accelerate convention next year in 2026!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 22:46:54','2025-07-01 22:46:54'),(15804,'judge-event-evaluation-21306-1751374536',21306,344,16,11,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7642,55,7888,6,'Collection',NULL,100,71.00,-10,-10.00,'First of all great job on a lovely poem. I\'m so sorry I had to give you negative 10 points since your poem was really good. Unfortunately the poem has to be between 8-32 lines, otherwise I have to give negative 10 points. And I counted and it came to 7 lines.\r\n\r\nSo hopefully next year, you will add 8 lines, so you wont have that negative score against you.\r\n\r\nAnyway, here is some feedback for you:\r\n\r\nThis poem has a heartfelt message and a clear spiritual focus that I found uplifting and comforting. The rhyme scheme is mostly consistent, and the theme of divine love and guidance is powerfully conveyed. However, the rhythm could be smoothed out in places—for instance, the third line feels slightly rushed due to its length compared to the others. Also, tightening the language (e.g., “our value our purpose and worth” might flow better with commas or rephrasing) would enhance clarity and impact. Overall, it’s a sincere and encouraging piece with room to grow rhythmically.\r\n\r\nThankyou so much for participating, and we can\'t wait to see you at accelerate conventions for 2026!\r\n\r\nPhilippians 4:13 - For I can do everything through Christ who gives me strength.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 22:55:36','2025-07-01 22:55:36'),(15805,'judge-event-evaluation-21383-1751375098',21383,344,16,11,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7676,55,7888,6,'Collection',NULL,100,78.00,-10,NULL,'This was such a beautiful piece, Jessira. We thankyou for going out of your way to submit this piece of art- a really great poem (Yes poetry is a form of art)\r\n\r\nHere is some criticism, both advice and what I loved about your poem.\r\nWhat Works Well:\r\n1. Clear Theme and Message:\r\nThe poem consistently centers on God’s Grace, conveying the idea that divine love and forgiveness are unwavering, even in the face of human failure. This gives it a strong thematic unity.\r\n\r\n2. Emotional Honesty:\r\nLines like “How many times I’ve failed” and “Oh, how wicked I’ve been” show vulnerability, which helps the reader connect with the speaker’s spiritual journey.\r\n\r\n3. Simplicity and Accessibility:\r\nThe language is clear and easy to understand, which works well for devotional poetry. This makes it accessible to a wide audience.\r\n\r\n-----\r\n\r\nSuggestions for Improvement:\r\n\r\n1. Repetitiveness vs. Reinforcement:\r\nWhile repetition can be powerful, the line “God’s Grace is enough” is used twice in close proximity with the same phrasing. Consider varying the wording or adding a twist to keep the reader engaged. For example:\r\n\r\nGod’s Grace holds firm through every trial,\r\nEnough to heal, enough to reconcile.\r\n\r\n2. Rhyme and Rhythm Tightening:\r\nSome rhyme pairs feel a bit forced or overly simplistic (e.g., “stuff” and “bluff”). Consider refining these to be more poetic or substituting richer, more evocative words.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\nOriginal: When man does wicked stuff\r\nPossible revision: When hearts grow cold and rough\r\n\r\n3. Line Breaks and Flow:\r\nThe rhythm is somewhat uneven in places. Reading it aloud can help you catch where the flow might stumble. You might want to experiment with syllable count or cadence in each line for a smoother reading experience.\r\n\r\nYou did a brilliant job, thankyou so much for your hard work in this poem, and hopefully I will see you around at accelerate next year for the next convention!\r\n\r\n1 John 2: 12- 14 (NLT I used but feel free to check it on any bible version- Id love if you could read this up!)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 23:04:58','2025-07-01 23:04:58'),(15806,'judge-event-evaluation-21058-1751375866',21058,344,16,11,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,8815,55,7888,7,'Collection',NULL,100,72.00,-10,-10.00,'When I read this I said to myself. \"What! An eleven year old wrote this!?\" I was shocked. Even though its so small its really powerful and impactful and would be a great story to share with kids at a kids church Sunday school.\r\n\r\nSadly I had to give you -10 points because the short story only had 570 words, while the minimum is 600. And you didn\'t list the numbers of words either.\r\n\r\nFrom me my only advice is to make it go a bit longer, and maybe you could  make the conflict seem a little more worse than you did.\r\n\r\nI especially loved the character, and how she gets her faith renewed, after talking to her friend, Melissa, because this really emphasizes what Jesus said when he said don\'t forsake the gathering of God\'s people. Chatting to God with a friend, is what builds faith, and I\'m glad you integrated it into your short story.\r\n\r\nI really do hope you will come back next year for accelerate conventions because this is really good, and I see a future author in you! Hope you have a fun time at this convention, and I pray God blesses you for the rest of the year!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 23:17:46','2025-07-01 23:17:46'),(15807,'judge-event-evaluation-21392-1751377905',21392,344,16,11,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,8845,55,7888,7,'Collection',NULL,100,69.00,-10,NULL,'Well done on a lovely book. My favorite character was especially Patch.\r\n\r\nGood stuff: The story is super cute and heartwarming! The characters are kind and brave, and the adventure feels fun and exciting. You did a great job showing how real friends help each other.\r\n\r\nWhat could be better: The middle of the story is a little slow, so maybe adding a tiny surprise or twist could make it even more exciting. Also, it might be fun to describe what Patch’s house looks like when they get there, to make the ending feel more complete.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-01 23:51:45','2025-07-01 23:51:45'),(15808,'judge-event-evaluation-20586-1751378630',20586,345,16,11,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,7350,5804,7888,7,'Collection',NULL,100,75.00,-10,NULL,'I love how your short story is a biography story. I\'m so sorry you felt homesick in Fiji, and I\'m glad you found your passion for drawing again through anime.\r\n\r\nThis is actually the first biography I have read that is entered in this category, and I applaud you on a job well done. There\'s not really any advice I can give you, because this is your story, and you would know more about it than me.\r\n\r\nKeep up the good work, and I hope you join ACE for the 2026 conventions. (Maybe even to enter your anime drawings in it)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-02 00:03:50','2025-07-02 00:03:50'),(15809,'judge-event-evaluation-20298-1751379040',20298,346,16,11,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,7175,4208,7888,7,'Collection',NULL,100,67.00,-10,-5.00,'Beautiful job! Keep up the good work. A suggestion would be to more clearly show the conflict, and how you resolved it more clearly. But other than that the story was great, showing the trials of friendships, and how we need to support each other through everything we do. I really hope you enter again next year. Sadly I had to deduct points because you did not state your word count. Keep smiling and shining always!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-02 00:10:40','2025-07-02 00:10:40'),(15810,'judge-event-evaluation-21239-1751379664',21239,344,16,11,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,7709,55,7888,7,'Collection',NULL,100,93.00,-10,NULL,'This short story was so thrilling, I wasn\'t bored and it kept me entertained the whole time. I am shocked someone who is 12 can write this good! You should write more books because I see a really big potential as a future fantasy author. And I even love how you integrated God, and that verse into the very end, this story about finding the light is powerful and amazing. One thing you could probably do to improve is to prolong the agony even longer for instance this bit: \r\nWhen she looked below, she saw a bunch of hungry piranhas waiting for someone to fall.\r\nJust as she was about to fall, a branch caught her shirt—\r\nBut then the branch broke. (You could mention more on how she\'s feeling suspended in mid air! And how she was feeling- is she terrified? Is she sad?)\r\nHer last words were, \"SOMEONE, ANYONE, PLEASE HELP ME!\" \r\n\r\nNice job, and I really hope you do ACE convention 2026 again, because you are really talented and have a true gift from God.\r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-02 00:21:04','2025-07-02 00:21:04'),(15811,'judge-event-evaluation-21388-1751380022',21388,344,16,11,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7698,55,7888,6,'Collection',NULL,100,71.00,-10,NULL,'Great poem, but perhaps next time you could add in some more rhyming and even more lines. Reading the poem out loud is a good idea before you submit, even though you might have done it you need to ask yourself does this sound quite right?\r\nI love how you mentioned Mr. flag as if he were a person but I did get confused near the end. Is Mr. flag mentioned in the end?\r\n\r\nYou did extremely well, especially for a boy at your age. And I\'m glad to see you back at convention this year! Hopefully next year too! God bless you, and have a great night. :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-02 00:27:02','2025-07-02 00:27:02'),(15812,'judge-event-evaluation-22141-1751404324',22141,344,16,11,3,2025,300,'924',NULL,8860,55,7759,45,NULL,NULL,0,0.00,NULL,NULL,'Did not attend',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-02 07:12:04','2025-07-02 07:12:04'),(15813,'judge-event-evaluation-21829-1751406295',21829,347,16,11,3,2025,352,'871','1',0,5806,7861,34,NULL,'28',100,99.00,-10,NULL,'Your hormones were beautiful and rich. Great job COC!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-02 07:44:55','2025-07-02 07:44:55'),(15815,'judge-event-evaluation-22243-1751406397',22243,344,16,11,3,2025,288,'908',NULL,7677,55,7847,44,'Collection','24',100,90.00,-10,NULL,'Well done. You really did express that passage well by using hand gestures and your facial expressions was good.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-02 07:46:37','2025-07-02 07:46:37'),(15816,'judge-event-evaluation-22243-1751406421',22243,344,16,11,3,2025,288,'908',NULL,7677,55,8800,44,'Collection','24',100,86.00,-10,NULL,'Good job! You showed great self-confidence. Your use of eye contact, pitch control, and tone variation was commendable. However, there were fewer gestures because you were holding the paper most of the time, which limited audience engagement.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-02 07:47:01','2025-07-02 07:47:01'),(15817,'judge-event-evaluation-21829-1751406466',21829,347,16,11,3,2025,352,'871','1',0,5806,7549,34,'Open','28',100,97.00,-10,NULL,'Thank you for that wonderful performance. We can hear clear balance in all the different parts. The beginning was beautiful with a strong ending. Well done COC! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-02 07:47:46','2025-07-02 07:47:46'),(15818,'judge-event-evaluation-21829-1751406644',21829,347,16,11,3,2025,352,'871','1',0,5806,7483,34,NULL,NULL,100,96.00,-10,NULL,'The message in the song was very well presented throughout the whole duration. The dynamics can be fine tune and the breathing at the interval are important that keep the life flow with he song. Thank you for the commitment that has shown through your presentation. God’s blessing be upon your endeavor.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-02 07:50:44','2025-07-02 07:50:44'),(15819,'judge-event-evaluation-21059-1751407150',21059,344,16,11,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,8823,55,7888,7,'Open,Collection',NULL,100,75.00,-10,-8.00,'I love you story, and how it was based on a real life experience seeing an angel. You must have been frightened. Thats a good thing God was looking out for you, to protect you from the dogs!\r\n\r\nMy only suggestion would be to make the story a tiny bit longer, because it didnt reach our 600 words minimum, and you didnt state the word count.\r\n\r\nI especially loved how you wrote the biography, yet still made it interesting, i never got bored once. Even some lines made me laugh. Such as the one where the bulldogs thought you were the last chicken nugget on earth! And your writing is really well done with other words similar.\r\n\r\nThanks so much for you short story submission, and I hope you will come back in 2026 for another year of ACE conventions!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-02 07:59:10','2025-07-02 07:59:10'),(15820,'judge-event-evaluation-21811-1751407392',21811,356,16,11,3,2025,300,'924',NULL,8880,4678,7756,45,'Collection','25',100,97.00,-10,NULL,'Great performance, Esther! Your confident delivery, clear voice, and expressive presence truly brought the poem to life. Just remember to incorporate more gestures to enhance your expression. Well done! \r\n\r\nVinaka.\r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-02 08:03:12','2025-07-02 08:03:12'),(15821,'judge-event-evaluation-21811-1751407395',21811,356,16,11,3,2025,300,'924',NULL,8880,4678,8702,45,'Collection','25',100,73.00,-10,NULL,'A lovey poem that reminds us to live life and not to rush through it. The only thing lacking from the delivery was characterization and incorporate that in next time for better results.  Good message & effort, Esther. Keep it up!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-02 08:03:15','2025-07-02 08:03:15'),(15822,'judge-event-evaluation-21811-1751407552',21811,356,16,11,3,2025,300,'924',NULL,8880,4678,7759,45,NULL,NULL,100,94.00,-10,NULL,'I like your poem, young girl. I think you are a bit nervous, right because it did affect your gestures. You are great at this and I hope that you will project your voice well next time and engage every one as you recite your poem. thank you.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-02 08:05:52','2025-07-02 08:05:52'),(15824,'judge-event-evaluation-22224-1751408000',22224,344,16,11,3,2025,352,'871','4',0,55,7549,34,'Open','28',100,88.00,-10,NULL,'Thank you for that 