7,'judge-event-evaluation-22318-1753734231',22318,404,22,22,3,2025,272,'855',NULL,6998,2720,5,32,NULL,NULL,100,95.00,-10,NULL,'You have a beautiful voice, keep using this gift for the glory of God who gave you it. Thank you for being brave! \r\nI hope to see you at another convention, read the guidelines re: memorizing lyrics and what needs to be provided to make sure you get maximum points there! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-29 06:23:51','2025-07-29 06:23:51'),(16848,'judge-event-evaluation-22318-1753734415',22318,404,22,22,3,2025,272,'855',NULL,6998,2720,6,32,'Open',NULL,100,93.00,-10,NULL,'Well done Hanna. Beautiful voice. Just some encouragement for future entries. Memorizing the lyrics will help with your hand movements and definitely be more comfortable. Other then that, well done again and we look forward to seeing future entries from you. God Bless.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-29 06:26:55','2025-07-29 06:26:55'),(16849,'judge-event-evaluation-22334-1753738778',22334,404,22,22,3,2025,313,'958',NULL,7005,2720,5,44,'Open','24',100,91.00,-10,NULL,'Well done, thank you for giving this event a go! I hope to see you at a future convention. If you try this event again, learn the reading a little more and it will help you to focus more on your actions and expressions. When you know whats coming next you can start to prepare for the next line. ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-29 07:39:38','2025-07-29 07:39:38'),(16852,'judge-event-evaluation-22345-1753739325',22345,404,22,22,3,2025,313,'958',NULL,8925,2720,5,44,'Open','24',100,89.00,-10,NULL,'Great job Robert, thanks for giving the event a try! I liked the subtle actions such as your mountain and water. If you do this event again in the future, try learning your chosen reading, I think you will then be able to do more expression and actions with it. Well done! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-29 07:48:45','2025-07-29 07:48:45'),(16853,'judge-event-evaluation-22345-1753739392',22345,404,22,22,3,2025,313,'958',NULL,8925,2720,6,44,'Open',NULL,100,82.00,-10,NULL,'Well done Robert. Some encouragement for future entries. Memorizing will help to the focus off from reading the script and focus more on your entry. Other then that, keep up the great work and God Bless.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-29 07:49:52','2025-07-29 07:49:52'),(16854,'judge-event-evaluation-22322-1753740107',22322,404,22,22,3,2025,330,'979',NULL,6998,2720,5,50,'Open','25',100,86.00,-10,NULL,'Thank you Hanna! Faith is so important, great topic. Next time, try to just have dot points in your outline and talk from those instead of reading. This will help you to connect with your audience more and speak from your heart. Take your time with illustrations to allow the audience to process and understand what your are sharing. Great job, keep sharing God\'s word with others. ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-29 08:01:47','2025-07-29 08:01:47'),(16855,'judge-event-evaluation-22322-1753740159',22322,404,22,22,3,2025,330,'979',NULL,6998,2720,6,50,'Open',NULL,100,90.00,-10,NULL,'Well done Hanna. Great message on faith and the important of it as well. One of my many favourite verses, without faith, it is impossible to please God. Just some encouragement, keeping eye contact with the congregation or crowd keeps them engaged with the message. Other then that, well done and keep on diving into His Word. God Bless.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-29 08:02:39','2025-07-29 08:02:39'),(16856,'judge-event-evaluation-22344-1753742449',22344,404,22,22,3,2025,353,'870','1',0,2720,NULL,34,'Open','27',100,92.00,-10,NULL,'Well done Imanuela Akatemia and Palmerston Luck. I really believe you have what it take to sing this at the other reginal conventions. Thank you for ministering to us and we pray God\'s blessings and favour over both schools. God Bless.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-29 08:40:49','2025-07-29 08:40:49'),(16858,'judge-event-evaluation-22344-1753742527',22344,404,22,22,3,2025,353,'870','1',0,2720,5,34,NULL,NULL,100,89.00,-10,NULL,'Well done Imanuela & Palmerston Lucky! This was so beautiful to listen to, definitely ministered to my heart. I know you were nervous, but next time try looking at your audience to connect with them. This is a group event, so give your best for your team mates! \r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-29 08:42:07','2025-07-29 08:42:07'),(16859,'judge-event-evaluation-22344-1753742691',22344,404,22,22,3,2025,353,'870','1',0,2720,6,34,'Open','27',100,93.00,-10,NULL,'Well done Imanuela Akatemia and Palmerston Lucky. I believe you have what it take to take this to other reginal conventions. Thank you for ministering to us and we pray God\'s blessings and favour over your two schools. God Bless.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-29 08:44:51','2025-07-29 08:44:51'),(16860,'judge-times-event-evaluation-22406-1753877832',22406,404,22,22,3,2025,34,'113',NULL,8897,2720,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,1,10,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,4,10,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-30 22:17:12',NULL),(16861,'judge-times-event-evaluation-22403-1753877832',22403,404,22,22,3,2025,34,'113',NULL,8893,2720,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-30 22:17:12',NULL),(16862,'judge-times-event-evaluation-22400-1753877832',22400,404,22,22,3,2025,34,'113',NULL,8902,2720,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,15,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-30 22:17:12',NULL),(16863,'judge-times-event-evaluation-22397-1753877832',22397,404,22,22,3,2025,34,'113',NULL,8896,2720,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,5,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-30 22:17:12',NULL),(16864,'judge-times-event-evaluation-22394-1753877832',22394,404,22,22,3,2025,34,'113',NULL,8926,2720,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,0,5,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-30 22:17:12',NULL),(16865,'judge-times-event-evaluation-22382-1753877832',22382,404,22,22,3,2025,34,'113',NULL,8929,2720,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,5,0,5,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,1,5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,15,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-30 22:17:12',NULL),(16866,'judge-times-event-evaluation-22379-1753877832',22379,404,22,22,3,2025,34,'113',NULL,8901,2720,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,0,5,0,NULL,0,NULL,1,20,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,2,15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,40,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-30 22:17:12',NULL),(16867,'judge-times-event-evaluation-22370-1753878185',22370,404,22,22,3,2025,62,'173',NULL,8925,2720,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,5,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-30 22:23:05',NULL),(16868,'judge-times-event-evaluation-22391-1753878250',22391,404,22,22,3,2025,78,'213',NULL,8928,2720,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,1,15,0,NULL,1,10,1,20,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,1,5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,50,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-30 22:24:10',NULL),(16869,'judge-times-event-evaluation-22388-1753878250',22388,404,22,22,3,2025,78,'213',NULL,8927,2720,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,5,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,1,5,1,5,NULL,NULL,15,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-30 22:24:10',NULL),(16870,'judge-times-event-evaluation-22385-1753878250',22385,404,22,22,3,2025,78,'213',NULL,8906,2720,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,5,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,1,20,0,NULL,1,15,0,NULL,1,5,3,20,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,65,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-30 22:24:10',NULL),(16871,'judge-times-event-evaluation-22376-1753878965',22376,404,22,22,3,2025,106,'273',NULL,6998,2720,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,1,NULL,1,20,0,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,3,20,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,70,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-30 22:36:05',NULL),(16872,'judge-times-event-evaluation-22413-1753878996',22413,404,22,22,3,2025,48,'143',NULL,7005,2720,6,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,1,20,0,NULL,1,20,1,30,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,2,15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,100,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-07-30 22:36:36',NULL),(16876,'judge-event-evaluation-22630-1755141271',22630,414,19,14,3,2025,186,'467','1',0,6097,8943,15,NULL,NULL,100,0.00,-10,0.00,'A creative rhyming story of Jonah. Well done for clear voicing and good sound effects :) Narrators were easily understood, and the story was easy to follow. A good message to leave us with at the end that God always knows best.\r\n\r\nEntry is missing some paperwork/info. 4x talent release forms, script, and nominated audience. (Nominated audience, eg. 8-12yrs, should be entered into the \"Context Box\" of the ACP.)\r\n\r\nTry adding some music for dramatic effect. An intro at the beginning to draw in the listener, and outro at the end to finish off. Also, musical interludes between scenes can help a story \'flow\' from one scene to the next :)\r\n\r\nMake sure script and voicing always line up with Scripture. In this audio, God\'s voice sounds like a female voice, but in the Bible God and His voice are always portrayed as masculine.\r\nIf all the actors want to be heard in the radio play and there are both females and males, choose a story with both female and male characters so it is in accordance with the guidelines and Scriptural principle :)\r\n\r\nA great team effort, well done on getting it together! :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-14 13:14:31','2025-09-04 07:56:33'),(16877,'judge-event-evaluation-22657-1755164678',22657,417,19,14,3,2025,21,'063',NULL,7580,4451,8943,7,NULL,NULL,100,91.00,-10,0.00,'A gripping, emotional story. You did a fantastic job of drawing the reader in from the start!\r\n\r\nThere is power in God\'s word. Try to incorporate a Bible verse, or base the story off a Bible verse then show how the story illustrates the truth of that verse. You have a good theme of God\'s love, it would be even stronger if you included a Bible verse/s as the foundation for the truth you\'re illustrating. For example, in John 8:32 Jesus says, \"And ye shall know the truth, and the truth shall make you free.\" You could incorporate that verse into the story, that she realized the truth of God\'s love and that is what made her free :)\r\n\r\nHad she accepted the sacrifice of her Messiah on the cross, and put her faith in the Lord Jesus Christ to save her from her sin? If yes, then she could have joyfully crossed over from this life of suffering and sorrow into His presence and eternal joy. Did she \'serenely roll into death\'s arms,\' or did she joyfully enter Heaven to be with Christ? :)\r\nAs believers, looking to Christ and our eternal future of joy with Him is one way we can endure suffering, and have hope in the midst of suffering. Romans 8:18 \"For I reckon that the sufferings of this present time are not worthy to be compared with the glory that shall be revealed in us.\" :)\r\n\r\nYour story had a very good presentation and visual appeal. One small thing you could try is to \'justify\' paragraphs that cover more than one or two lines. Justifying means to align both sides of the text evenly. It is not always necessary, but is usually a good idea and can give an even tidier appearance :)\r\n\r\nGreat effort! And well done on a great story. Keep writing and using your gift for God! :) :) :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-14 19:44:38','2025-08-14 19:44:38'),(16878,'judge-event-evaluation-22628-1755839031',22628,417,19,14,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,7322,4451,8943,6,NULL,NULL,100,80.00,-10,0.00,'Well done for writing a poem about such a worthy topic! :) I like the symbolism of the \'open road to Heav\'n\' and \'Jesus paving the way\' analogy.\r\n\r\nIt is effective that you begin with the problem (sin) then move to the solution (the Lord Jesus Christ). The repeated verse is effective as well.\r\nGiven the nature of the poem, you could begin with the repeated verse, then continue repeating it throughout as a refrain to reinforce your main message.\r\n\r\nTry shifting some words around to help it flow a bit better.\r\nFor example, instead of \"With us ALL being BUT lost,\" it could read, \"With us being ALL BUT lost.\"\r\nAlso, \'For this WE DO pray,\' it would flow better to say, \"For this DO WE pray.\"\r\n\r\nWell done for a neat poem :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-22 15:03:51','2025-08-22 15:03:51'),(16879,'judge-event-evaluation-22632-1755847478',22632,414,19,14,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,7898,6097,8943,6,NULL,NULL,100,74.00,-10,0.00,'Well done for writing this poem on kindness. Kindness is a great Biblical theme :)\r\n\r\nTry to include an attribute of God for the quality you are encouraging. For example, the kindness and love of God... Which he shed on us abundantly through Jesus Christ our Saviour (Titus 3:4,6). All of the things God wants us to be(eg. kind), He is, and we have a strong foundation for our message when we start from that viewpoint :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-22 17:24:38','2025-08-22 17:24:38'),(16880,'judge-event-evaluation-22654-1755848094',22654,417,19,14,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,7576,4451,8943,6,NULL,NULL,100,85.00,-10,0.00,'Great poem! Very engaging, you drew me in right from the start :)\r\nVery good descriptive language, \'showing\' rather than telling, excellent work!\r\n\r\nDouble check that all lines begin with a capital letter.\r\n\r\nTry to avoid breaking up verses with commas. Each verse should complete it\'s own thought :)\r\n\r\nA pleasure to read, keep writing and using your gift for God! :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-22 17:34:54','2025-08-22 17:34:54'),(16881,'judge-event-evaluation-22641-1755849117',22641,417,19,14,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,8940,4451,8943,6,NULL,NULL,100,85.00,-10,0.00,'Well done for writing an engaging, descriptive poem!\r\n\r\nSome of the lines are not aligned consistently, make sure to double check little details like this :)\r\nYou could remove the comma on line 7, as the phrase is continued onto the next line. A helpful way to know whether you need punctuation at the end of a line is to ask yourself, \"Would I include a comma in this phrase if it was continued on the same line?\" \r\nFor example, \"But by the God who protects us,\" not, \"But by the God, who protects us.\" :)\r\n\r\nBecause the thought of the poem continues until the end, you could present the poem as one paragraph. :)\r\n\r\nThe use of contrasts is very effective. Great work! Keep writing and using your gift for God :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-22 17:51:57','2025-08-22 17:51:57'),(16882,'judge-event-evaluation-22607-1755850057',22607,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7318,4451,8943,6,NULL,NULL,100,98.00,-10,NULL,'Great work Grace!\r\n\r\nYour poem was a pleasure to read!\r\n\r\nDescriptive and engaging, you draw the reader in and hold their attention til the end.\r\n\r\nFantastic topic, well set out, and very well written. Keep writing and using your gift for God! :D <3',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-22 18:07:37','2025-08-22 18:07:37'),(16883,'judge-event-evaluation-22597-1755850532',22597,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7316,4451,8943,6,NULL,NULL,100,100.00,-10,0.00,'WOW!!! Holly I LOVE your creativity, and the ADORABLE little story you have crafted based on the little fish from Matthew 17! Super super cute, very fun :)\r\n\r\nYou are very gifted, and it is great to see you using that talent for the Lord! Keep writing and giving God glory! :) :) :) God bless you!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-22 18:15:32','2025-08-22 18:15:32'),(16884,'judge-event-evaluation-22610-1755850936',22610,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7317,4451,8943,6,NULL,NULL,100,95.00,-10,-5.00,'Laura I LOVE your poem! Very well written and thought-provoking. You are very talented, and it is such a blessing that you are using your gift for the Lord. :)\r\n\r\nSome marks were lost as a result of the poem being outside the 8-32 line limit, but other than that it is an AMAZING poem!!!\r\n\r\nKeep writing and using your gift for God!!! God bless you!!! :) :) :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-22 18:22:16','2025-08-22 18:22:16'),(16885,'judge-event-evaluation-22605-1755851828',22605,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,8908,4451,8943,6,NULL,NULL,100,91.00,-10,0.00,'Well done, Roshanna! This is a delightful poem expressing the wonders of God\'s creation :) It reminds me of Psalm 104.\r\n\r\nFor the concluding phrase, it is fantastic and effective as is. Could be improved if you made it rhyme, to fit with the rest of the poem :)\r\nSpelling is superb. One point was deducted for one word, \'Monkey,\' which was missing an \'s\' to make it plural :)\r\n\r\nVery well done, keep writing and using your gift for God! May God bless you abundantly!!! :) :) :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-22 18:37:08','2025-08-22 18:37:08'),(16887,'judge-event-evaluation-22615-1755854025',22615,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7327,4451,8943,6,NULL,NULL,100,92.00,-10,0.00,'A fun descriptive poem celebrating God\'s creation. Well done Savannah!\r\n\r\nA couple things to improve:\r\n1. Double check that all verbs agree in tense. For example, the poem is written in present tense, but the river \'rushed\' past, when it needed to be \'rushes.\'\r\n\'Rushes\' also helps the poem\'s rhythm \'flow\' better :)\r\n\r\n2. The phrase, \"Bees and worms in the sky and ground,\" could be stated more clearly as, \"Bees in the sky and worms in the ground.\"\r\n\r\nGood work, keep writing and using your gift for God! God bless you! :) :) :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-22 19:13:45','2025-08-22 19:13:45'),(16888,'judge-event-evaluation-22596-1756107065',22596,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7575,4451,8943,6,NULL,NULL,100,85.00,-10,0.00,'Whew! Such a lot of noise! :) Could be a picture book! :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-25 17:31:05','2025-08-25 17:31:05'),(16889,'judge-event-evaluation-22614-1756258480',22614,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7806,4451,8943,6,NULL,NULL,100,70.00,-10,0.00,'Wow what a creative idea to write a poem about dirt bikes!\r\nYou did a good job of \'showing\' what was happening. There is a lot of visual language which is fantastic! :)\r\n\r\nIs there a way you could tell how riding dirt bikes glorifies God? Perhaps one of the verses could thank God for dirt bikes? :)\r\n1 Cor. 10:31 Whether therefore ye eat, or drink, or whatsoever ye do, do all to the glory of God.\r\nColossians 3:17 And whatsoever ye do in word or deed, do all in the name of the Lord Jesus, giving thanks to God and the Father by him.\r\n\r\nBe consistent with your verb tenses. Is the poem meant to be present tense or past tense? Either way is ok, you just need to choose one and stick with it all the way through :) Always double check for spelling mistakes too :)\r\n\r\nThe poem needs consistent rhyme. Your line at the end of the first verse is neat, it contains three words that rhyme and fit a good meter. Perhaps you could try doing that for all four verses and follow the pattern of having three rhyming words for the last line of each verse.\r\n\r\nWell done for writing a poem, Brooklyn! Keep writing and God bless you as you use your talents for Him! :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-27 11:34:40','2025-08-27 11:34:40'),(16890,'judge-event-evaluation-22616-1756260123',22616,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7324,4451,8943,6,NULL,NULL,100,85.00,-10,NULL,'What a fun poem! :) You\'ve got great rhyme and tell a great story!\r\n\r\nIs there a way you could show how enjoying a day at the beach glorifies God? Perhaps the children could thank God for the wonderful sunshine and sand and water He created :)\r\n\r\nThe theme, as indicated by the title, is about a day at the beach, but in verse four they go to the park. Try to stay consistent with the theme :) Alternatively, you could simply rename the poem with an all-encompassing title and that would be fine as well :)\r\n\r\nGenerally, each verse of a poem should end with a full stop. A new paragraph indicates a new sentence/phrase/idea. Small but watch out for that :)\r\nAlso, make sure there\'s a space between the title/author and the beginning of the poem :)\r\n\r\nKeep writing, God bless you as you use your gifts for Him!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-27 12:02:03','2025-08-27 12:02:03'),(16891,'judge-event-evaluation-22606-1756275463',22606,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7329,4451,8943,6,NULL,NULL,100,86.00,-10,NULL,'A neat poem about a day on the beach! You\'ve done a great job of rhyming words, and \'showing\' us what you saw :)\r\n\r\nDouble check your verb tenses, and stay consistent throughout the poem. Is it past tense or present tense? Either is fine, just make sure you choose one and stick with it :)\r\n\r\nMake sure to have a space between the title/author and the first line of the poem :)\r\n\r\nIs there a way you could show how enjoying the beach glorifies God? Perhaps a verse thanking God for the beach and the fun times you have there?\r\n1 Cor. 10:31 Whether therefore ye eat, or drink, or whatsoever ye do, do all to the glory of God.\r\nColossians 3:17 And whatsoever ye do in word or deed, do all in the name of the Lord Jesus, giving thanks to God and the Father by him.\r\n\r\nKeep writing! God bless you as you use your talents for Him! :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-27 16:17:43','2025-08-27 16:17:43'),(16892,'judge-event-evaluation-22604-1756333039',22604,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7573,4451,8943,6,NULL,NULL,100,78.00,-10,0.00,'What a neat poem Sophie! You give glory to God, and celebrate the beauty and strength of a horse running free :)\r\n\r\nPerhaps you could find some synonyms (different words with similar meanings) to make it more creative. For example, the horses could run \'unfettered,\' and \'unhindered,\' etc. Are they muscular? Perhaps we could see their strong muscles rippling as they run.... Synonyms can make the message more interesting and expressive :)\r\n\r\nGreat work Sophie, keep writing and using your gift for God! :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-28 08:17:19','2025-08-28 08:17:19'),(16894,'judge-event-evaluation-22628-1756458480',22628,417,19,14,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,7322,4451,7314,6,NULL,NULL,100,93.00,-10,NULL,'Thank you, Braden, for entering this event.  You have made a superb effort to ensure that your poem has a 7576-syllable pattern in your verses of poetry.  You have also followed an ABAB rhyme pattern.  I especially enjoyed the effective use of the shortened version of \'Heaven\' so that your syllable pattern was met.  \r\nWork on proof reading and editing a bit more closely, I picked up two spelling/typing errors - grith/girth, an/and.\r\nI love your repetition of verse 3 it sounded melodic, and I can imagine what you wrote as a song.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-29 19:08:00','2025-08-29 19:08:00'),(16896,'judge-event-evaluation-22641-1756460372',22641,417,19,14,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,8940,4451,7314,6,'Open',NULL,100,68.00,-10,NULL,'Thank you, Tobie for writing your poem.  You have used easily understood language to write your poem.  This poem is technically correct and could be spiced up with a rhyme pattern.  You used a 4-syllable pattern throughout your poem, well done.  There is a comparison implied between the storms of life and a storm \'.   You have been creative with your contrasts that you have used.  ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-29 19:39:32','2025-08-29 19:39:32'),(16897,'judge-event-evaluation-22632-1756461457',22632,414,19,14,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,7898,6097,7314,6,'Open',NULL,100,77.00,-10,NULL,'Well done, Heidi!  I especially took note of the way you used semicolons to extend the pauses between associated ideas; this really helped with the flow of the poem.   You used a rather free form approach to your poem and the repetition worked well. The poem would have benefited the reader if between each verse there was some white space to create a break between ideas and concepts.  Also consider meter and rhyme to be included in your poems.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-29 19:57:37','2025-08-29 19:57:37'),(16899,'judge-event-evaluation-22614-1756507705',22614,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7806,4451,7314,6,'Collection',NULL,100,75.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Brooklyn, I loved the way you used some very descriptive and exciting language.  We are so blessed that we have the opportunity to do what we enjoy in our leisure time and pursue our passions and interests.  It is always exciting to see how God may use your dirt bike riding in the future.  There are a few grammatical and some punctuation errors.  The meaning of line 3 is not clear to me.  Some ways you can enhance your writing is to create rhyme and rhythm with the syllables in your verse structure.  Your writing shows a lot of promise, and I look forward to reading more of your work in the future.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-30 08:48:25','2025-08-30 08:48:25'),(16900,'judge-event-evaluation-22602-1756509040',22602,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7577,4451,7314,6,'Collection',NULL,100,75.00,-10,NULL,'Thanks, Callum, for your poem.\r\nYou have written a good rhyme pattern (AAAA BBBB CCCC DDDD} each verse having its own individual word to rhyme with this shows you have a good sense of rhyme and pattern.  To enhance your poem when you present it you could leave 4 lines between each verse, it does not matter if it goes on to another page as long as it reaches the guidelines.  You have used some simile in you writing, well done.  It is great to have a hobby and collecting things is a lot of fun.  We do need to look into the history of hobbies in some cases as they may be based in things that do not line up with Biblical principles.  I can see that you were very selective in what language you did use which shows that you have some discernment in your content choice for your audience.  \r\nYou kept 11 syllables per line through the whole poem, well done.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-30 09:10:40','2025-08-30 09:10:40'),(16901,'judge-event-evaluation-22616-1756509800',22616,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7324,4451,7314,6,'Collection',NULL,100,61.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Charlie,\r\nIt is always lovely to go to the beach and enjoy God\'s creation.  Thank you for writing about this.\r\nYou have used an ABAB rhyme pattern and 6,6,7,7 syllable pattern throughout your poem.  Awesome effort.  There needs to be a gap in your presentation between by Charlie Oliver and the first line of your poem otherwise it blurs into the title.  Some small punctuation errors.  End each verse with a full stop.  When writing we can enhance what we have written by adding some lively adjectives and adverbs.  I look forward to reading future poems you may write and see your development.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-30 09:23:20','2025-08-30 09:23:20'),(16902,'judge-event-evaluation-22607-1756510493',22607,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7318,4451,7314,6,'Collection',NULL,100,91.00,-10,NULL,'Thank you, Grace, for your poem.  It definitely meets the purpose of being evangelistic, Biblical, Christian and yes even historical.  It is very fit for purpose.  Amazing effort!  You kept to a 7,8-syllable pattern in all your verses except for verse 5 which was an 8,7-syllable pattern.  There also are a few small punctuation errors.  Using some simile and personification has enhanced some of your verses.  Well done!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-30 09:34:53','2025-08-30 09:34:53'),(16903,'judge-event-evaluation-22597-1756511713',22597,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7316,4451,7314,6,'Collection',NULL,100,91.00,-10,NULL,'Thank you Holly for an excellent poem that drew me into the watery world of a fish below the sea with the imagery and the personification of the fish in the tale you told.  You used an ABCB rhyme pattern throughout your poem with great skill.  Your syllable patterns were there but harder to find as you varied them a little but they were repeated again later in the poem.  You are learning to manipulate language for purpose well done.  I imagined that the voice the fish heard was the voice of God.  Very in keeping with the Bible story the Fish and the Coin.  Whether the coin came from the South I did not know but a great way to end the poem.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-30 09:55:13','2025-08-30 09:55:13'),(16904,'judge-event-evaluation-22610-1756512319',22610,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7317,4451,7314,6,'Collection',NULL,100,95.00,-10,-5.00,'Laura an amazing poem that is based on 8 lines in a verse with an 8-syllable pattern right the way through followed by a single line verse of 6 syllables.  Such form and control are admirable and effective.  Unfortunately, the poem was definitely not between 8 and 32 lines and was quite a bit over (45 lines).  The poem though really was written well and the 45 lines only added to the effectiveness of the poem, so I had to take off half the marks allocated.  This poem is worthy of a command performance.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-30 10:05:19','2025-08-30 10:05:20'),(16905,'judge-event-evaluation-22596-1756513774',22596,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7575,4451,7314,6,'Collection',NULL,100,95.00,-10,NULL,'Wow Paige, I love it!  This poem would make and amazing children\'s book.  I know my 2-year-old grandson would love this.  The repetition enhances and you have very cleverly used an AABB rhyme pattern.  Your syllables in each line vary a bit but each first line of each verse starts with 8 syllables.  Reading through though the variation is not a problem and still works.  One missed comma is the only thing I could pick up.  I am looking forward to seeing a book on the shelf that perhaps has the noises to go with it. (His dad is a builder!)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-30 10:29:34','2025-08-30 10:29:34'),(16906,'judge-event-evaluation-22605-1756514590',22605,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,8908,4451,7314,6,'Collection',NULL,100,87.00,-10,NULL,'Roshanna, you have painted a picture of animals everywhere which links to you final 2-line verse about God\'s creation at the end of the poem.  This poem is fit for purpose, well done.  A small grammatical error monkey/monkeys and you chose to use no punctuation at the end of each line.    I loved the form of a 4-syllable line, followed by a five-syllable line, followed by a six-syllable line and finishing with a 7-syllable line.  Very clever.  I also enjoyed the fact you used an AABB rhyming pattern for each verse except your last verse.  This created a good contrast, highlighting the main point.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-30 10:43:10','2025-08-30 10:43:10'),(16907,'judge-event-evaluation-22615-1756515391',22615,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7327,4451,7314,6,'Collection',NULL,100,86.00,-10,NULL,'Savannah this poem is short and sweet, but in it you have painted a beautiful picture for the reader.  It is amazing that when we sit in the peacefulness of nature it links us with our creator, when we observe how detailed God was with everything, we find we are amazed at the pattern, beauty and mathematics of his design.  I can see that you find your peace in what God has created.  I would like to see some more poetic devices incorporated.  Each verse has an 8585-syllable pattern. You have used an ABCB rhyme pattern.   Punctuation is accurate.  ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-30 10:56:31','2025-08-30 10:56:31'),(16908,'judge-event-evaluation-22606-1756516687',22606,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7329,4451,7314,6,'Collection',NULL,100,76.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Sofia,\r\nYou have made an excellent effort to rhyme the end of your lines following an AAAA BBBB CCCC DDD pattern. You have described an idyllic New Zealand beach scene like the one I was used of as a child and young adult.  I loved the beach and still do, your passion for your subject comes through in your writing.  Some things to work on in the future is your verb form and subject agreement as well setting a syllable pattern that will give rhythm to your poem.   A lovely effort, looking forward to reading some more poetry next year.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-30 11:18:07','2025-08-30 11:18:07'),(16909,'judge-event-evaluation-22604-1756517421',22604,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7573,4451,7314,6,'Collection',NULL,100,73.00,-10,NULL,'Sophie, what passion you have written with.  I can tell you love horses very much and appreciate God\'s creation of them.  I can see you have attempted a rhyme pattern and a syllable pattern, keep working on this as it will enhance your writing in your future endeavors.  When presenting your work make sure that there are 4 line space between your verses so that it defines each verse clearly.  Use a full stop at the end of each verse.  You have used emotive language, and I can see that you appreciate the beauty of one of God\'s creatures wild and free.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-30 11:30:21','2025-08-30 11:30:21'),(16910,'judge-event-evaluation-22626-1756518511',22626,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7578,4451,7314,6,'Collection',NULL,100,68.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Vanessa,\r\n\r\nIt is always good to write poetry when something or someone is close to our heart.  When we lose someone, it helps us process this.  Having the promise of Heaven is a comfort to those on earth as we know we will see our loved ones someday.  Thank you for sharing these emotions with me in poetic form.  I know the feelings are deep.  \r\nWorking on Meter, rhythm and a regular rhyme pattern would make this poem very effective.  Counting syllables can help with this.  Also make sure that when you format you leave spacing between the verses so that they can be clearly seen by the reader. Be consistent with your punctuation.\r\nMost of the best poetry comes from the heart and draws on the inner persons thoughts and actions.  Keep on writing and developing this area as you have a lot to offer the world from your experiences.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-30 11:48:31','2025-08-30 11:48:31'),(16911,'judge-event-evaluation-22654-1756518767',22654,417,19,14,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,7576,4451,7314,6,'Open',NULL,100,81.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Jacob,\r\nA very sincere poem that conveys raw emotion.  I could totally relate to the poem you have written, except it would be titled, \'The Girl in the Field.\"  You free formed your poem which makes it easier to write, and there is a place for this, not usually where there are strict marking guidelines.  At Student Convention the poem has 15 marks allocated to meter, rhythm and rhyme.  You effectively wrote a 5757-syllable pattern but there was no evidence of rhyme. An area to work on would be use of comas and capitals in poetry.  You painted a beautiful picture through your imagery and use of simile.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-08-30 11:52:47','2025-08-30 11:52:47'),(16913,'judge-event-evaluation-22626-1756675090',22626,417,19,14,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7578,4451,8943,6,NULL,NULL,100,87.00,-10,0.00,'Great poem Vanessa! It is poignant, yet filled with hope at seeing the departing loved one again :)\r\n\r\nTry to keep the verses a consistent length, for example 6 lines each :)\r\n\r\nKeep writing and using your gift for God! :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-01 07:18:10','2025-09-01 07:18:10'),(16914,'judge-event-evaluation-22629-1756677196',22629,417,19,14,3,2025,8,'014',NULL,7573,4451,8943,8,NULL,NULL,100,80.00,-10,0.00,'Well done for writing a book report Sophie! I can see you put a lot of effort into writing it! You\'ve described the characters very well :)\r\n\r\nIs there a Biblical principle you learned from the story? Perhaps you could include a paragraph about that :) Is it kindness to animals(Pro. 12:10)? Or families working together and valuing each other(John 13:34)? Or perhaps it could be how God sometimes takes away one thing to give us something better, as when Vicki said goodbye to one pony but then got Dandy. Any Biblical principle is ok, just make sure to include a paragraph or a few sentences about it :)\r\n\r\nGood effort, God bless you! :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-01 07:53:16','2025-09-01 07:53:16'),(16915,'judge-event-evaluation-22658-1756678095',22658,417,19,14,3,2025,8,'014',NULL,7329,4451,8943,8,NULL,NULL,100,0.00,-10,-2.00,'Conflict with Biblical worldview. One of the characters lies to be \'kind\' to her friend and it seems to be portrayed as a positive thing.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-01 08:08:15','2025-09-04 21:39:53'),(16919,'judge-event-evaluation-22688-1756679454',22688,414,19,14,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,8913,6097,8943,7,NULL,NULL,100,91.00,-10,-7.00,'WOW Benjamin! What an AMAZING story! You drew me in and held me captive from the beginning til the end. You are a gifted storyteller and it is a HUGE blessing to see you using that gift to honour your Creator in the days of your youth.\r\n\r\nMake sure to include the word count, \'justify\' the paragraph alignment, and use double spacing :)\r\n\r\nOne thought, you\'ve done a FANTASTIC job of showing how Jesus came to die for the lost, it could be a tiny tad clearer as to how to accept that gift by coming, or believing. Simply reading the Bible and knowing the truth is not enough, one must believe to be saved. While you hint at that, and it is VERY effective, you could state it a bit more clearly :)\r\n\r\nAmazing story, WELL DONE!!! :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-01 08:30:54','2025-09-01 08:30:54'),(16922,'judge-event-evaluation-22613-1756685489',22613,417,19,14,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,7329,4451,8943,7,NULL,NULL,100,67.00,-10,0.00,'Whew! I feel hungry!\r\nThis was a fun story Sofia :) I can see you put a lot of thought into writing it! It is an interesting scenario, for an unsaved person to be trapped on an island with a Christian :)\r\n\r\nTry to think about the story you\'re creating and make the details agree with each other :) For example, if the two men hadn\'t had enough food for so many days, would they have had the energy to jump up when the rescuers arrived? Would they have grabbed their things and RUN to the boat, or would they have rejoiced when the rescuers arrived and then collapsed after the strain of surviving for so long? :)\r\n\r\nYou could possibly include a bit more about the interaction between the two men. Did they have any meaningful or significant conversations? How were they feeling when they were on the island? How did each of them help the other survive and get through the difficulty? :)\r\n\r\nKeep an eye out for paragraph alignment. You can \'justify\' the paragraph, meaning both sides of the text are aligned and give a tidy appearance :)\r\n\r\nWell done for writing this story, great effort! Keep writing and using your gifts for God! :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-01 10:11:29','2025-09-01 10:11:29'),(16923,'judge-event-evaluation-23085-1756685930',23085,414,19,14,3,2025,180,'461',NULL,7922,6097,7888,11,'Open',NULL,100,80.00,NULL,NULL,'Really good job, the painting looks lovely, and I love all the shading and lighting you managed to put in the image. It is very hard to add so much of that, and you did it brilliantly, thankyou!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-01 10:18:50','2025-09-01 10:18:50'),(16924,'judge-event-evaluation-23231-1756686137',23231,414,19,14,3,2025,180,'461',NULL,8919,6097,7888,11,'Open',NULL,100,78.00,NULL,NULL,'Great job, I love you art. Maybe next time you can make the moon more crescent maybe. I especially loved how well you did the clouds, and the detail you put into the flower! You did a good job, and keep up the good work! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-01 10:22:17','2025-09-01 10:22:17'),(16925,'judge-event-evaluation-23045-1756686390',23045,417,19,14,3,2025,180,'461',NULL,7733,4451,7888,11,NULL,NULL,100,90.00,NULL,NULL,'I really love this piece. I especially love how it sort of pops out like it was almost a 3-D model. It was shaded beautifully and you did a wonderful job! Great job on a lovely piece of work! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-01 10:26:30','2025-09-01 10:26:30'),(16926,'judge-event-evaluation-22688-1756686786',22688,414,19,14,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,8913,6097,7888,7,'Collection',NULL,100,84.00,-10,NULL,'I really enjoyed the story, although there wasn\'t really a big conflict, you did so well in writing the story, and it kept me drawn in the whole time, I did not look away. Thanks so much for entering this, I think you should share this story with the world, keep shining and may God bless you!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-01 10:33:06','2025-09-01 10:33:06'),(16927,'judge-event-evaluation-22627-1756690915',22627,417,19,14,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,7327,4451,8943,7,NULL,NULL,100,81.00,-10,-2.00,'What a lovely story Savannah! You have done a great job writing a story about loving your neighbour as yourself. I would love to be welcomed to the neighbourhood with baking and a church invite :)\r\n\r\nTry adding some paragraphs to enhance the story\'s readability :) For example, the first paragraph could be introducing the main character.\r\nThe second paragraph could describe the new neighbours.\r\nThe next paragraph could be about going to the shop to buy the cake mix.\r\nThe fourth paragraph could be making the cake.\r\nAnd so on :)\r\n\r\nWatch out for grammar, and stay consistent with verb tenses :)\r\nA little bit more punctuation would be good too. For example, if you\'re thinking something, add a \',\' then quotation marks (\" \") on either side of the thought. See sentence below.\r\n--I thought, \"I finally have some new neighbours!\" I was very excited.--\r\n\r\nBreaking up a thought into two sentences can be helpful, and can add to the story. For example, \"I saw that we had new neighbours and I was very excited,\" could become, \"I saw that we had new neighbours! I was very excited.\"\r\n\r\nGreat effort Savannah! Keep writing and using your gifts for God! God bless you! :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-01 11:41:55','2025-09-01 11:41:55'),(16929,'judge-event-evaluation-22631-1756691261',22631,417,19,14,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,7573,4451,8943,7,NULL,NULL,100,64.00,-10,0.00,'Great effort Sophie! You\'ve written an action packed, dramatic story!\r\n\r\nKeep an eye out for your paragraph spacing. Sometimes there\'s a paragraph break in the middle of a sentence. It\'s a good idea to re-read and check little details like that before submitting :)\r\n\r\nSome of the story details tend to be a bit unclear. For example, if the Christians were expecting \'them\' to come after them for their faith, would they still be meeting publicly and openly?\r\nMusic stands and band members indicate a modern day setting, so it would be unusual for the family to be riding in a wagon...\r\nChoose a time and place for the setting of your story, and think about how all the details should line up with that time and place :)\r\n\r\nYou did really well with using different words, and not just \'he said, she said.\' You used words like \'stated,\' and \'shouted,\' to make it more interesting, well done!\r\nJust make sure that written out conversations have a new line for each reply. See example below.\r\n\r\nDad asked Mum, \"What\'s for dinner?\"\r\n\r\nMum replied, \"Sausages and beans.\"\r\n\r\n\"That sounds yummy!\"\r\n\r\n\"Thank you dear.\"\r\n\r\nGood work Sophie, keep writing and using your gifts for God! :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-01 11:47:41','2025-09-01 11:47:41'),(16931,'judge-event-evaluation-22623-1756697461',22623,417,19,14,3,2025,185,'466','1',0,4451,6,14,NULL,NULL,100,90.00,NULL,NULL,'Great start on your site Luke James Rout. The content is clear and well thought out. A few small tweaks — like fixing typos, adding a sticky menu or back-to-top button, and organizing sections more clearly - would make navigation super smooth. You’re definitely on the right track, keep it up and God Bless.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-01 13:31:01','2025-09-01 13:31:01'),(16933,'judge-event-evaluation-22658-1756751614',22658,417,19,14,3,2025,8,'014',NULL,7329,4451,7314,8,'Collection',NULL,100,0.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Sofia,\r\nIt looks like you really understood the characters in this book, and you have given a good description of each one you chose.  A small error in grammar was picked up: him/his.  You are well within the word count.  Although you have not clearly explained the Biblical principal learned you have mentioned Biblical principles of kindness and empathy.\r\nYou also mention the uncomfortableness of the main character in the situation he has been put in and I could see that the setting was a school.  You have given a decent description of the characters and there is some character analysis evident.\r\nThere is no in-depth analysis of the theme.   Your length of paragraphs is appropriate and you are well within the word count.  I do not know whether you read a book or watched a movie to write this book report.  Your final statement in your report says that you really enjoyed this movie.    1 Samuel 16 vs 7 is a good verse to give when you are connecting it to the book \"Wonder\" as it says that \'God does not look at the outward appearance but he looks at the heart.\'    I can see that the theme of this book and the contents really spoke to you.\r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-02 04:33:34','2025-09-04 21:39:53'),(16935,'judge-event-evaluation-22629-1756752826',22629,417,19,14,3,2025,8,'014',NULL,7573,4451,7314,8,'Collection',NULL,100,80.00,-10,NULL,'I can see Sophie that you are passionate about horses.  You chose a story that is set in New Zealand, and you described the setting and the characters well. The characterization descriptions you gave were arranged in a logical order and gave me as the reader an insight into the book.  Next time remember to give a clear explanation of the Biblical Principal learned in this book which would have been based around stewardship, looking after what God has given us.  Noah was a great steward for God when he took the animals onto the ark and looked after them well.  Be careful with using capital letters in your name.  There were some wrong tenses used in you writing used:  fed and feed. spelling rid/ride.  A grammar/spelling check on your writing will help with this in the future.  Thank you for your amazing insights into this book. It would have been a book I would have read when I was your age and loved.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-02 04:53:46','2025-09-02 04:53:47'),(16937,'judge-event-evaluation-22659-1756758546',22659,419,19,14,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,8934,8346,8943,7,NULL,NULL,100,95.00,-10,0.00,'WOW Marni! You\'ve written a great story, fast moving and action packed. I LOVE the theme of not letting phones get in the way of real relationship. Super important and you did a great job of writing about it :D\r\nSuperb presentation! You aligned the paragraph edges, and even added a footer! Very good :)\r\n\r\nWatch out for run on sentences! A long sentence can often be broken up into several, or if need be, use commas/colons/dashes :)\r\n\r\nI LOVE that she wanted to share Jesus with her new friend! :) A full gospel message needs to include our sin problem, and what the Lord Jesus Christ did to solve it. He came from Heaven to Earth to die as the payment for our sin, was buried, and rose again. If we believe in Him and accept His free gift of forgiveness, THAT\'S when we\'re born again and receive eternal life :) See 1 Cor 15:1-5. Also, beware of basing faith on feelings and not God\'s Word (I know you included Lisa sharing the Bible and that\'s fantastic! Feelings will follow true faith but our foundation must be the what God has said and not a feeling.) :)\r\n1 John 4:10, \"Herein is love, not that we loved God, but that he loved us, and sent his Son to be the propitiation for our sins.\"\r\nActs 16:31, \"And they said, Believe on the Lord Jesus Christ, and thou shalt be saved, and thy house.\"\r\n\r\nA delightful story, very well written. Well done! :) Keep writing and using your gifts for God! :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-02 06:29:06','2025-09-02 06:29:06'),(16940,'judge-event-evaluation-22611-1756760117',22611,417,19,14,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,7317,4451,8943,7,NULL,NULL,100,89.00,-10,0.00,'Well done for an engaging story Laura! I can see you put a lot of thought and effort into writing it :)\r\nYou do a wonderful job of \'showing\' and describing where the story is and what is going on.\r\n\r\nI LOVE the idea of following the story of one particular shepherd! Very creative, and a nice angle that many people may overlook :) I think the story would be more powerful if he went with the others and met the baby Jesus, and that could be a resolution to his conflict.\r\n\r\nMake sure to check your paragraph alignment. You can \'justify\' your paragraphs so that both edges are evenly aligned :) You have fantastic paragraph spacing though, and it is double spaced and very readable, which is fantastic :)\r\n\r\nWell done Laura! Keep writing and using your imagination and talents for God! :) God bless you!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-02 06:55:17','2025-09-02 06:55:17'),(16942,'judge-event-evaluation-22619-1756761373',22619,417,19,14,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,7316,4451,8943,7,NULL,NULL,100,98.00,-10,NULL,'Wow Holly! What an interesting story from the book of Speculations :) You\'ve written an engaging story, and I can tell you put a lot of time and thought into writing it :)\r\n\r\nExcellent job with your paragraph spacing and presentation!\r\n\r\nBe aware of all the details in the time and place of your story\'s setting. For example, I\'m pretty sure Saul and his friends would be wearing robes, so would they have been walking on their hands? And would they have pockets in a boy\'s robe? Possibly. You\'ve thought about and written details which is FANTASTIC! Just be aware and think of ALL the details :)\r\n\r\nIt\'s a very interesting thing to think about the backstories of Biblical heroes. Saul was definitely a zealous persecutor of Christians before he got saved and became the Apostle Paul. However, from what he says later on in his life, it sounds like he was more zealous for the \'true\' religion and the honour of God, rather than a bitterness toward the Christians. Galatians 1:11-14, Philippians 3:4-6, Acts 22:3 KJV. Just a thought :)\r\n\r\nI love how you set us up for the climax at the Damascas Road :D\r\n\r\nGreat effort Holly, well done! Keep writing and using your imagination and talents for God! God bless you!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-02 07:16:13','2025-09-02 07:16:13'),(16948,'judge-event-evaluation-22620-1756765077',22620,417,19,14,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,7318,4451,8943,7,NULL,NULL,100,95.00,-10,0.00,'Well done for a descriptive and visual story Grace!\r\nYou made good use of adjectives and \'showed\' us where things were happening :) Good job!\r\n\r\nI can see that you put a lot of time and thought into writing it. You\'ve done some research into the time the story is set in too, and some of the cultural things they would do at a Jewish wedding. That is fantastic! I particularly noticed the messenger inviting them, that is a good detail that makes the reader think about a time before emails and texting :)\r\n\r\nExcellent double spacing! Try to break up the text into some paragraphs to enhance readability.\r\nWatch for text alignment too, you can \'justify\' your paragraphs so both sides of text are aligned evenly :)\r\n\r\nBeware of \'me and...\' You wrote it correctly once with, \'my brothers and I...\'\r\nJust watch that each time there are multiple people that you write it as, \'so-and-so and I.\' :)\r\n\r\nFun fact, in Bible times they measured time starting at 6am, so 11am would be \'the fifth hour.\'\r\nThe gospels mention \'the sixth hour,\' which is midday, 12pm, and \'the ninth hour,\' which is 3pm :)\r\nMatthew 20:1-6; 27:45, Mark 15:33, Luke 23:44, John 4:6, John 19:14 KJV\r\n\r\nGreat effort Grace! Keep writing and using your imagination and talents for God\'s glory! God bless you! :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-02 08:17:57','2025-09-02 08:17:57'),(16950,'judge-event-evaluation-23031-1756765928',23031,417,19,14,3,2025,173,'451',NULL,7322,4451,9155,2,'Open','5,8',100,77.00,-10,NULL,'This is a lovely photo idea, to draw the eye down the path. I know it can be tricky to get the lighting right in such environments, but you\'ve managed to capture that quite well. \r\nWhat let\'s the photo down, however, is possibly the resolution. The image is grainy, which could be from blowing it up a little in the printing, or it could be from using the zoom when capturing it (zoom on phones aren\'t great).\r\nKeep developing your photography skills!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-02 08:32:08','2025-09-02 08:32:09'),(16951,'judge-event-evaluation-23098-1756766561',23098,414,19,14,3,2025,173,'451',NULL,7901,6097,9155,2,'Open','5,8',100,69.00,-10,NULL,'The composition of the animals is good with the pigs in the foreground, and the rooster walking towards them, which draws the eyes towards the main subject of the pigs.\r\nIt looks like the photo is taken out of a car window. Unfortunately the quality of the image is not very good and this could perhaps be because it was taken as a moving shot. The camera will not have had much time to focus on any particular element and it could further have acquired a more granny image when it was blown up since the quality of the original was not that great. When trying to take a nice photo to display, consider taking it from different angles to get the elements in the best arrangement, and also consider taking it from a stationary position so that the camera has the opportunity to capture everything well.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-02 08:42:41','2025-09-02 08:42:41'),(16952,'judge-times-event-evaluation-22575-1756766674',22575,417,19,14,3,2025,42,'137',NULL,7576,4451,7871,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,5.36,5.36,4.84,4.37,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-09-02 08:44:34',NULL),(16953,'judge-times-event-ev