ion, I want to understand if you drew this artwork, because Canva is a graphic design program, not for drawing and therefore it is impossible to produce digital art in the program without its drawing tools. I love your idea of the artwork, so make sure that you submit it correctly according to the event you chose. Thank you.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 06:39:35','2025-10-06 06:39:35'),(19476,'judge-event-evaluation-25242-1759697585',25242,439,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,7053,4679,9287,11,'Collection',NULL,100,96.00,NULL,NULL,'Please make sure to find and write the name of the owner for the image you found as the source.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 06:53:05','2025-10-06 06:53:05'),(19477,'judge-event-evaluation-28550-1759697646',28550,461,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,9138,7991,9287,11,'Collection',NULL,100,89.00,NULL,NULL,'Please make sure to find and write the name of the owner for the image you found as the source.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 06:54:06','2025-10-06 06:54:06'),(19478,'judge-event-evaluation-26590-1759697700',26590,463,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,9100,5934,9287,11,'Collection',NULL,100,97.00,NULL,NULL,'Please make sure to find and write the name of the owner and the link address for the image you found as the source.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 06:55:00','2025-10-06 06:55:00'),(19479,'judge-event-evaluation-27824-1759697842',27824,461,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,8278,7991,9287,11,'Collection',NULL,100,85.00,NULL,NULL,'Please make sure to find and write the name of the owner and the link address for the image you found as the source. In addition, next time you can describe the step-by-step procedure with more details, such as I colored the background first with blue, then sketch the bird standing on a tree branch, then colored it with base colors, and so on until the result.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 06:57:22','2025-10-06 06:57:22'),(19480,'judge-event-evaluation-28551-1759697911',28551,461,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,9141,7991,9287,11,'Collection',NULL,100,94.00,NULL,NULL,'Please make sure to find and write the name of the owner for the image you found as the source.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 06:58:31','2025-10-06 06:58:32'),(19481,'judge-event-evaluation-26593-1759698024',26593,463,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,9082,5934,9287,11,NULL,NULL,100,88.00,NULL,NULL,'If possible, write what kind of contest for your theme idea next time and a link address for it.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 07:00:24','2025-10-06 07:00:24'),(19482,'judge-event-evaluation-24573-1759698063',24573,430,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,7602,392,9287,11,'Collection',NULL,100,90.00,NULL,NULL,'Please make sure to find and write the name of the owner and the address link for the image you found as the source.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 07:01:03','2025-10-06 07:01:03'),(19484,'judge-event-evaluation-26594-1759714642',26594,463,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,8081,5934,8535,11,'Collection',NULL,100,52.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Amadeus, I like your idea depicting the sunset, and you can make it even better by smoothly blending your gradients and adding more details and shading! Keep learning and improving, Amadeus.\r\n\r\nP.S. Please fill in your reports and documentation more seriously next time :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 11:37:22','2025-10-06 11:37:22'),(19485,'judge-event-evaluation-26578-1759714671',26578,463,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,8090,5934,8535,11,'Collection',NULL,100,74.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Abigail, I like your interpretation of the Armor or God, the designs are interesting and your anatomy is pretty good too! However, the lack of detail and colors in the background held back the potential of your artwork. The textures you used also seemed somewhat arbitrary, as if used in the wrong places. Overall, you have a lot of potential! Keep drawing and don\'t give up on those backgrounds ;) I hope to see you again next year with an even better artwork, good job Abigail!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 11:37:51','2025-10-06 11:37:51'),(19486,'judge-event-evaluation-26470-1759714748',26470,461,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,9130,7991,8535,11,NULL,NULL,0,0.00,NULL,NULL,'Did not attend',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 11:39:08','2025-10-06 11:39:08'),(19487,'judge-event-evaluation-25318-1759715507',25318,458,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,7420,4200,8535,11,'Collection',NULL,100,79.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi, Angellina, you\'ve got some skills! I love your style and the technical skill you\'ve displayed, I can tell you\'ve been drawing for quite some time :) It would be a lot better to display your skills on a more interesting drawing/story rather than a simple portrait, I know you can do a lot more with those skills! Rendering more could do you some good, making your drawing clearer and sharper to guide the viewer\'s eyes to the focal point. Don\'t be afraid to be bolder with your shadows, too, it creates good contrast to add interest. Overall, you have a lot of potential, so keep drawing and improving and I hope to see you again next year with an even better artwork! Nice work, Angellina ;)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 11:51:47','2025-10-06 11:51:47'),(19488,'judge-event-evaluation-26961-1759716080',26961,473,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,8228,3716,8535,11,'Collection',NULL,100,78.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Austin, I really like the way you drew the fire and its light! It looks very convincing, however the rocks in the foreground made it less convincing as the shadows and lighting are a bit off. The trees in your background could use some better shapes to make it look more convincing, too. Overall, your artwork is good, and I can see you have potential! Keep drawing and cultivating your skills, and I hope to see you again next year with an even better artwork! Good job, Austin :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 12:01:20','2025-10-06 12:01:20'),(19489,'judge-event-evaluation-26584-1759716913',26584,463,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,9084,5934,8535,11,'Collection',NULL,100,75.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Avery! Your lotus and butterfly looks beautiful :) I liked the color variation you used, but the lack of shadows hold back the potential of your artwork. Don\'t be afraid to put down shadows to make your artwork more convincing, and you can add more details with sharper lines to make your artwork look clearer. You\'ve done a good job overall, keep learning, especially in shading, and I hope to see you again next year with an even better artwork! Nice work, Avery!\r\n\r\nP.S. Don\'t scribble on your reports next time, you can write with pencil or write slower to avoid mistakes, it\'ll make your documentation look neater ;)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 12:15:13','2025-10-06 12:15:13'),(19491,'judge-event-evaluation-27156-1759725592',27156,439,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,9009,4679,8535,11,NULL,NULL,100,61.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Axel, your artwork is very neat! It\'s also very simple, and while that may not be a bad thing, it prevents you from displaying a lot of shading, perspective, contrast, and technical skills in your artwork. I can see you\'re an diligent and thorough person, so I\'m sure you can improve a lot in digital art if you put your mind to it. You have an art sense that you can develop, so keep growing and keep learning, Axel :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 14:39:52','2025-10-06 14:39:52'),(19492,'judge-event-evaluation-25746-1759726065',25746,439,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,9014,4679,8535,11,'Collection',NULL,100,53.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Bryan, I like your idea to depict nature, and maybe you can depict it a lot better if you had a reference to help you. You have a good imagination, you just have to develop your technical skills to showcase your imagination into your artwork using better shapes, colors, shading, etc. Keep learning more and you can improve, Bryan :) ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 14:47:45','2025-10-06 14:47:45'),(19493,'judge-event-evaluation-26484-1759726496',26484,461,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,9132,7991,8535,11,NULL,NULL,0,0.00,NULL,NULL,'Did not attend',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 14:54:56','2025-10-06 14:54:56'),(19494,'judge-event-evaluation-24455-1759727929',24455,464,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,8187,1009,8535,11,NULL,NULL,100,76.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Chloe, I didn\'t expect to see Frisk in a Convention artwork submission haha ;) I like how well you displayed the mood through your artwork, and I really like how you drew the clouds! I think your artwork looks just a bit muddy though due to slight overuse of the airbrush, especially using a small airbrush. Aside from that your technical skills are pretty good, keep drawing and keep improving, Chloe, and I hope to see you again next year with an even better artwork!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 15:18:49','2025-10-06 15:18:49'),(19495,'judge-event-evaluation-25170-1759729422',25170,430,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,7596,392,8535,11,NULL,NULL,100,58.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Chris, your artwork is very neat! It\'s also very simple, and while that may not be a bad thing, it prevents you from displaying a lot of shading, perspective, contrast, and technical skills in your artwork. I can see you\'re an diligent and thorough person, so I\'m sure you can improve a lot in digital art if you put your mind to it. You have an art sense that you can develop, so keep growing and keep learning, Chris :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 15:43:42','2025-10-06 15:43:42'),(19496,'judge-event-evaluation-25246-1759735467',25246,439,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,8019,4679,8535,11,NULL,NULL,100,51.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Clarence, you have a good imagination, you just have to develop your skills to match your imagination through improved use of shapes, linework, colors, shading, etc. Keep learning and improving, Clarence :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 17:24:27','2025-10-06 17:24:27'),(19498,'judge-event-evaluation-24000-1759736577',24000,447,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,9066,6328,8535,11,'Collection',NULL,100,70.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Elliott, I like all the details you drew in your artwork! Although some details and some parts look a bit messy, overall your train looks nice. One thing that might be holding back your art is your shading, as good shading can really level up your art, learn more about shading and lighting, and I hope to see your again next year with an even better artwork, maybe a better train haha ;) Keep improving, Elliott!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 17:42:57','2025-10-06 17:42:57'),(19499,'judge-event-evaluation-27692-1759736618',27692,473,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,7932,3716,8535,11,NULL,NULL,0,0.00,NULL,NULL,'Did not attend',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 17:43:38','2025-10-06 17:43:38'),(19510,'judge-event-evaluation-25028-1759748699',25028,430,21,7,3,2025,346,'865','1',0,392,9290,36,'Open',NULL,100,93.00,NULL,NULL,'Well done Kevin. This is a great arrangement that you have submitted for a 4-part vocal ensemble. I will provide feedback on all aspects where you were not given full marks.\r\nIA. The variety in harmony that you have given us lies in the arrangement of voices, not the harmony itself. It would have been nice to have heard more variety in the actual harmony itself, not just in the interludes that were composed, but also going alongside with the melody.\r\nIB. Rhythmically, the triplets are an interesting and nice change and variation - however, the polyrhythms in this setting detract from the song rather than add. I would instead keep triplet figures to be consistent across all 4 voices, unless some are holding long notes across the whole triplet. I am mostly referring to bars 68 and 70. \r\nIC. Whilst the arrangement is technically very good, it does not bring it into a \"unique composition\". You composed an interlude which was unique, however you did not arrange part of the songs for it to become completely unique. If you had even added one more reharmonisation to the actual song, this would\'ve been given full marks undoubtedly.\r\nIG. They were definitely pleasing and melodic, but similarly to IC, lacking in originality, outside of the composed parts.\r\nII. Dynamically, you used adding and removing different voices, which worked very well. For more interesting ideas, use crescendos, decrescendos, accents and volume indicators such as piano, forte, etc. \r\nIVB. The performance was good, but not perfect. There is no room to hide with a cappella when it comes to intonation, so be on the lookout for that. Make sure that phrases end at the same time, especially when rests are there. \r\nOverall, you did a very good job on the arrangement of this piece. It can be difficult to arrange a piece like this which already has quite a rich harmony, but you tackled it well and focused on the movement of inner voices, which was very good. If you were to choose a piece like this again, see where you can add more originality within harmony, and with any other piece, remember to focus on dynamics as well.\r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 21:04:59','2025-10-06 21:04:59'),(19511,'judge-event-evaluation-26613-1759751900',26613,463,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,8132,5934,NULL,5,NULL,NULL,100,67.00,-10,0.00,'Strong attempt at a strong topic. You\'ve used references and Scripture well, and have valid points. However, your writing structure, flow and choice of words has limited the delivery.\r\n\r\n1st sentence is already a poor and failed start to any persuasive writing: you should not assume everyone knows. The point of a persuasive essay is to state your strong argument, define the points and reason why, and not use your assumption of the reader\'s knowledge. Your second sentence unpacks it slightly, but the role of a 1st sentence -- especially in the opening of the essay -- is to immediately capture the reader\'s attention and introduce the essay\'s topic and overall direction.\r\n\r\nSimilar to the above, you need to make sure that in all your opening sentences are a strong statement that will be well supported by the sentences that follow. The opening sentence for paragraph 2 states that there are a lot of cases, but you only used 1 example.  In 3rd paragraph, you introduce that there are 2 perspectives (Biblical\'s and world\'s) but you address the world\'s perspective in the next paragraph -- as suggested in your opening sentence in paragraph 4. In sentence 5, there is no closing sentence that brings home (summarises) the point of that sentence to persuade the reader, only a reference statement that strengthens your argument. The role of a reference statement is to support your point, not argue for you.\r\n\r\nParagraph 6 started of strong, with good supporting sentences. However, from the sentence starting with \"Such correction...\", you are contradicting yourself. You used the example of someone taking time to reflect, but then later you say that the timing does not matter. You also used the reason of  correction to be delivered gently, then later you argue that inappropriate method of correction is does not matter. By the end of paragraph 6, you have failed to deliver a counterargument, because your statements instead support your original argument. \r\n\r\nYour closing paragraph is emotionally persuasive, but has not referenced the points used throughout your essay. It uses emotion-based language to \"pull the heart strings\', but it does not play its part in providing persuasive reasoning to tie it together. It introduces \"true happiness\" which has not been clearly discussed earlier on. Your thesis statement in the opening and the end does not match up: the first is supporting self-growth, the end closes on the \"right judgement\" in your interactions with others. So either this sentence is poorly constructed, or it does not match up with the outline.\r\n\r\nIt\'s also not good to definitive language in a persuasive essay such as \"obviously impossible\', \"it is clear\", and \"ultimately\", because your role as a writer is to justify why, not just state it.\r\n\r\nOutline does not have consistent sentence structure and does not follow the ACE standards of outline writing (see guidelines).\r\n\r\nI think your points have strong validity and potential, but they have not been organised and written in a way that makes the reading easy to follow. I\'d recommend focusing more on in less points and making them stronger.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 21:58:20','2025-10-06 21:58:20'),(19519,'judge-event-evaluation-25632-1759756804',25632,447,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,9069,6328,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,62.00,-10,0.00,'Hi Felicia,\r\n\r\nI think you\'ve chosen a very interesting topic -- incredibly relevant with potential to be strongly driven towards one perspective. Your outline is also strongly written, which consistent sentence structure. However, I would recommend using the outline structure as suggested in the student convention guidelines. \r\n\r\nHowever your writing has missed the format and context of the persuasive essay writing event. The point is to open your first paragraph with a strong thesis, use the following paragraphs to state 1 point each (under which you use supporting sentences to persuade the reader), then use the closing paragraph to summarise your points and persuade your reader towards your argument.\r\n\r\nHowever, your opening paragraph gave me a history of the nations, which should be covered in paragraph 2, similar to what you have done with the background of Israel. Without reading your outline, I still would not have known what you are persuading me towards. The title should only be a teaser to what your point is. There is no clear topic point stated in the opening sentence, therefore it\'s hard to understand what you\'re trying to persuade. You have a strong last sentence at the end, but that still doesn\'t answer the topic (if assuming you were attempting the title to be the arguing topic).\r\n\r\nAfter reading the essay, I\'m also left questioning to where Palestine comes into play. You\'ve unpacked about Israel\'s history, but not Palestine\'s. I understand that there are more Scriptural references about Israel, however, if you are writing about the two countries, then there must be equal history for both (even if you need to search beyond just from Scripture). \r\n\r\nI can see what you are trying to tie together (the history of Israel to seeing their reality today), however your writing skills have not been able to support the deliver your intention. I would suggest working on the fundamentals of essay writing (which is the same as what I\'ve suggested above), and then aiming to tackle a simpler topic incredibly well. All the best.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 23:20:04','2025-10-06 23:20:04'),(19520,'judge-event-evaluation-26621-1759757066',26621,446,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,9060,2276,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,55.00,-10,-9.00,'Hi Annabelle, \r\n\r\nGreat try on tackling an incredibly strong topic. I can see your train of thought and the points you find relevant to the topic. However, I do think that you need to improve on your fundamental essay writing skills. I would suggest tackling a simpler topic, and doing incredibly well at that!\r\n\r\nThere was a lot points stated, but not persuasive enough. There are sentences that tells the reader they are \"foolish\" and \"wrong\"; however, the essay should instead persuade, argue and educate the reader to WHY those views are wrong. In other words: quoting Scripture is important, but this essay hasn\'t written their argument persuade the reader. \r\n\r\nYou have also gone on tangents that do not support the key points. Here\'s an example: Paragraph 2 is arguing what the Bible says about homosexuality, but you ended the paragraph on body surgery. While the topic of the design of human body may be relevant, it does not align to the point you\'re trying to make and the essay outline. If you think discussing bodies is relevant in your essay, it should\'ve been in a separate paragraph.\r\n\r\nIn the future, after you write a strong statement or quote a Scripture/reference, follow it up with a supporting sentence or two that justifies why your strong statement or reference makes a strong reason. It\'s better to pick 2-3 strong points and create strong arguments that support each point. Then remember to start and end each paragraph to support that statement. Each paragraph should only discuss 1 point. Otherwise you end up rambling...\r\n\r\nPoints deducted as formatting is not double spacing, length of essay is below 500-100 requirement, and word count not stated.\r\n\r\nI hope this has been helpful. All the best for your next essay!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 23:24:26','2025-10-06 23:24:26'),(19524,'judge-event-evaluation-26606-1759758993',26606,463,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,8158,5934,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,84.00,-10,0.00,'Hi Felicia,\r\nThis is such an interesting merge of topics and very unique argument to tackle! Great work at it! Your language is consistent, your arguments are strong and convincing.\r\n\r\nThe areas of improvement would be in your writing structure and outline, essentially the fundamentals of essay writing. \r\n\r\nYour opening sentence to the essay should be capture the reader\'s attention, establish the general topic, and set the tone for the paper by drawing the reader into the introduction and preparing them for the essay\'s argument. You\'ve done the attention and teased for the topic well, however, it doesn\'t tell me what the essay is about. You also frequently refer to Gen Z, but assumes the reader knows the exact years of Gen Z and the Indonesian context of Gen Z (I don\'t!). You mentioned Labubu as an example, but I\'m left trying to understand if that is within the Indonesian context or not.\r\n\r\nI would suggest your first paragraph providing basis of what your thesis statement is and a high level overview of the points you are going to make to justify why this will be a good argument. Then your second paragraph gives context (the stats, definition of Gen Z in Indonesian context, the trends etc). Then the rest of the paragraphs provide 1 clear point each, which strong supporting statements, and a strong closing statement. \r\n\r\nAn example is your sentence 3 does not follow the above structure, and therefore does not tell me what your main arguing point is. It touches on a few valid points, but the opening and closing sentence does not align. It feels like 2 train of thought that are relevant to each other but put into 1 sentence. \r\n\r\nYour outline does not meet the student convention guidelines structure of an outline. It should not have the opening hook, thesis statement and conclusion in sentences written -- that\'s the point of the essay. Having \"details\" is also irrelevant to the structure of the outline. If you understand the correct structure of an online, then you\'ll see how the subheadings plays the part of breaking down details.\r\n\r\nStill, compelling writing. All the best for your next one!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 23:56:33','2025-10-06 23:56:33'),(19525,'judge-event-evaluation-26567-1759759114',26567,461,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,8303,7991,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,65.00,-10,-4.00,'Hi Audrey, \r\nThis is quite a unique topic, and from the start you have a very clear direction of your argument - which is great! Unfortunately, you have missed the opportunity to deliver it home. \r\n\r\nYou used a lot of big words and strong points, but fail to strongly justify the \"why\'s\". The essay left an impression that you have statements to support your perspective, but not persuade why one should agree with you. \r\n\r\nParagraph 2 has a valid opening sentence, but the closing sentence (or even second sentence) does not strengthen the opening sentence. Leading into the next paragraph is a good attempt, but it doesn\'t help when the paragraph itself doesn\'t have a strong point. \r\nIn paragraph 3, you introduced your three points, but do not define what they are. Your writing assumes the readers have the same thinking and definition of those factors as you. You missed the \"what\" and went straight to the \"why\", both are crucial in persuasive writing.\r\nParagraph 5 & 6 have overlapping points. You introduce \'stability\' in paragraph 5 but only unpack it in paragraph 6. You make a lot of big statements in paragraph 5, but the reasoning needs to be strengthen. 1 sentence per statement doesn\'t persuade the reader enough for such a big topic, it just gives the reader a direction of your thinking. Considering you still have a lot of quota in your word count, you could\'ve strengthen a lot of your statements.\r\n\r\nOutline is clear and logically written, however the sentence structure in the points are not consistent.\r\n\r\nPoints deducted as word count is not stated, and many grammar mistakes (words missing, punctuation incomplete or incorrectly used, incomplete sentences).\r\n\r\nIn the future, I would suggest picking simpler points that you can strongly support (rather than big points that you have many details and end up mentioning a little about a lot). You don\'t need to discuss everything, but the things you discuss must be discussed well :) ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 23:58:34','2025-10-06 23:58:34'),(19526,'judge-event-evaluation-26613-1759759160',26613,463,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,8132,5934,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,68.00,-10,0.00,'Good attempt at a difficult topic, however the writing structure, choice of words, and flow has limited the potential of the delivery. I\'d suggest working on your writing skills before tackling a challenging topic. It\'s better to write a strong, convincing, persuasive essay on something simpler, than not being able to do well on a complex topic. The below are points in your writing that will hopefully help you do better in the next one.\r\n\r\n1st sentence in the opening is already a mistake in any persuasive essay: do not assume that everyone knows. Your reader may not! I can see that you tried to address it in the second sentence, but by falsely assuming, you are giving a gap in your argument that doesn\'t need to exist. The role of the 1st sentence -- both for the beginning of an essay and each paragraph -- should capture the reader\'s attention, establish the general topic, and set the tone for the essay.\r\n\r\nYou\'ve done a great job defining what judgement is - very strong and clear. The paragraph is simply written and effective. Great use of references.\r\n\r\nSimilar to the previous point, you need to work on ensuring that each of your opening sentences direct the points of your paragraphs, and then well justified by supporting sentences. Like in Paragraph 3, you state that there are \"a lot of cases\", but you only used 1 example. In paragraph 4, you introduce in the first sentence that there are 2 perspectives (Biblical\'s and the world\'s). However you only unpack about the world\'s perspective in paragraph 5 -- or as suggested by your opening paragraph. \r\n\r\nYour closing sentences should also conclude and deliver home the point you are making in each sentence. In paragraph 5, you conclude with a reference. However, a reference should provide validity to your argument as a support, but it does not argue your point for you. \r\n\r\nI would also suggest refraining from using strong definitive language like \"obviously impossible\" or \"It is clear\". The role of a writer is to persuade the reader as to why and how, not just state that it is obvious. It also assumes that the reader can see why it is obvious without taking the time to say why.\r\n\r\nIn paragraph 6, you started with a great opening and following sentences. However, the paragraph goes on a tangent as it does not follow a clear line of thought. It compares content vs. context, which may be relevant but a side-step from the point. \r\n\r\nFrom a Biblical worldview perspective, the following sentence is not true nor accurately used, \"The most truthful message, even if it is conveyed at the wrong time or through an inappropriate method, is unlikely to foster one’s personal and spiritual growth.\" The middle phrase, suggests that the delivery does not matter, but the rest of your paragraph argues that it does. The rest of the sentence, being, \"The most truthful message ... is unlikely to foster one’s personal and spiritual growth,\" is not correct as the word \"truth\" can include topics such as salvation, Jesus\' death and resurrection, and Creation. I think you are trying to convey something else but have missed the mark. \r\n\r\nLastly, your closing paragraph does not bring it home. It uses a lot of emotional language to persuade the reader, however, it does not bring together strongly the points used throughout the essay. It also introduces \"true happiness\" which has not been unpacked in the paragraphs above. The closing sentence also fails to conclude the argument by answering \"self-growth\" or \"self-righteousness\", but it compares right from wrong -- the comparison does not line up to the opening thesis.\r\n\r\nI\'d encourage you to use this essay feedback to learn the fundamentals of strong essay writing and furthermore your critical thinking skills :)\r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-06 23:59:20','2025-10-06 23:59:20'),(19527,'judge-event-evaluation-26603-1759760811',26603,463,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,9114,5934,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,71.00,-10,-1.00,'Hi Gracelyn, Strong topic choice, and great work on staying focused on theme. I am left wanting to read more! I have some points below that could\'ve helped with your argument.\r\n\r\nAn opening sentence of an essay, and the beginning of each paragraph, should capture the reader\'s attention, establish the general topic, and set the tone for the paper by drawing the reader into the introduction and preparing them for the essay\'s argument. Your first and second sentence are worded very similarly, both mention social media, but the key points of your essay is not about social media. Unfortunately your \'hook\' has played a misleading role. A hook is nice to have if done well, but more of a journalism style of writing, not persuasive.\r\n\r\nFor a topic this complex, it would\'ve help your case if you expanded more on the history of feminism, what it looked like and achieved, and then what it actually looks like today and how it has progressed. You\'ve made bold statements, but haven\'t taken the time to unpack them and even spell out what it looks like in reality. You still have a lot of word count quota that could\'ve been used to strengthen your essay.\r\n\r\nYou\'ve referenced big concepts, but lack in giving context to support your reasoning. For example, a sentence you used like, \"Today, feminism is viewed as a weapon to hurt others, when that was not its purpose.\" As a reader, I\'m asking, \"how is it viewed as a weapon?\" \"What are the modern examples can I relate to?\" \r\n\r\nThere is slight inconsistency in the tone of your writing, where the sentences about feminism uses complex and nuanced language, while the parts that relates it to scripture uses simpler phrasings. \r\n\r\nYour outline is also not adhering to the student convention guidelines. The sentence structure must be consistent throughout the whole outline (bullet point phrases that summarises your argument point, not sentences or half sentences). You also don\'t spell out the hook, background information and thesis statement in the outline. The reference page should also always be left-aligned, despite the essay being centred aligned. \r\n\r\nI hope this helps your future writing! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 00:26:51','2025-10-07 00:26:51'),(19538,'judge-event-evaluation-26255-1759800535',26255,446,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,9058,2276,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,73.00,-10,-2.00,'Hi Jaden, great work on putting together a personalised persuasive essay! The essential points you chose to support your topic were focused, very relevant and logical. Your outline is strong, and follows a very clear line of thinking. Then the execution of your essay follows the outline very well. Your flow and progression between paragraphs worked together very smoothly.\r\n\r\nHere are some suggestions to help your future writing:\r\nConsider including your topic (or thesis statement) in the first paragraph. I see your title eludes to it, but the point of the first paragraph is to spell out and establish what you are trying to persuade the reader. \r\n\r\nI would also strengthen each paragraph by sharpening your closing sentence. Each opening and closing sentence in each paragraph should work together: the opening introduces the point you\'re making, and the closing sentence strongly restates your point. The middle sentences should support the opening, and justify the closing. You\'ve done well with the opening sentences of each paragraph, but your closing sentences need to strongly summarise and persuade the reader. \r\n\r\nThen similarly, your closing paragraph plays the part to strongly persuade the reader - tie it together and bring it home! I can see that your writing tone gets more encouraging, but I would suggest adding a couple more sentences in the middle of the last paragraph that pulls together all the points you have made in your previous paragraph. \r\n\r\nWell done, and all the best with your future writing. \r\n\r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 11:28:55','2025-10-07 11:28:55'),(19544,'judge-event-evaluation-26590-1759801786',26590,463,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,9100,5934,8535,11,NULL,NULL,100,92.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Lovine, your artwork looks great! I really like the technique you used to draw it, not to mention with a mouse haha, I know that pain well :\') I love all the subtle color variations you displayed in the fur, it really makes the subject come to life. Nicely done, Lovine, keep drawing and getting better, explore deeper into art, such as more daunting perspectives, dynamic lighting, poses, and more! I hope to see you again next time with an even better artwork, I\'ll be cheering you on as a fellow art kid :) See you on top, Lovine!\r\n\r\nP.S. Hope you can use your Wacom again soon ;)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 11:49:46','2025-10-07 11:49:46'),(19545,'judge-event-evaluation-27820-1759801857',27820,461,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,9194,7991,8535,11,'Collection',NULL,100,90.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Danica, your artwork is very good! I love how you drew the bird with all its color variety, as well as the bokeh effect in the background, very well done! If you could maybe detail either the bird or the flowers in the foreground a bit sharper, that would be perfect. Other than that, you\'ve done a really good job! Keep drawing, keep getting better, and I hope to see you again next year with an even better artwork, see you on top, Danica :) ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 11:50:57','2025-10-07 11:50:57'),(19546,'judge-event-evaluation-27691-1759801982',27691,473,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,7932,3716,8535,11,'Collection',NULL,100,93.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Felice, I really like your artwork! I love all the patterns, colors and textures on the coat and fur, nicely done! I can see you have a good grasp of shading and textures, one thing you can improve on is drawing facial features and hair. Aside from that, you\'ve done very well, I\'ll be cheering you on as a fellow art kid :) Keep learning and improving, and I hope to see you again next time with an even better artwork, see you on top, Felice!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 11:53:02','2025-10-07 11:53:02'),(19553,'judge-event-evaluation-27033-1759802358',27033,433,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,8975,5317,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,80.00,-10,-5.00,'Hi Jillian,\r\n\r\nImpressive writing for such a complex topic! Your reasoning is strong, your points are persuasive and supported with strong arguments. I enjoyed reading it and felt educated by your research.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, you have been deducted points in areas that could\'ve been avoided:\r\n- You\'ve provided a summary of your intention of the essay, but not an outline. Please look at the student convention guidelines for what an outline should be. This is also unfortunate, as having an outline would have supported you in ensuring your structure is better formed and your points logically ordered.\r\n- Deduction for passing 1000 word limit and word count not stated. \r\n- References not correctly written, and formatting should always be left aligned for a bibliography.\r\n\r\nIn terms of constructive feedback:\r\nYou have used very strong points that strengthen your argument, however the structure and flow of how you\'ve organised your paragraphs could be improved. It\'s worth spending time on an outline to list how you will break down each essential point, and how your points support them. Paragraph 2 & 3 reads like it should be one paragraph; yet paragraph 4 reads like it should be supporting sentences for the point you\'re making in paragraph 4. Your 5th paragraph is an excellent example of how to do it well: You started with a strong point, justified it with research and lived experiences, and then your closing sentence strongly summarises the conclusion of that point.\r\n\r\nI would also avoid using demonstrative pronouns at the beginning of a sentence(eg: \"this view\", \"this defense\"). The point of an opening sentence of each paragraph is to introduce to the reader what your key point (it should also match up to the point written in your outline). So if a paragraph starts with \"... supports this view,\" then the reader is left asking \"what view?\" I can see later that you are referring to the previous point, but opening with \"this\" starts the paragraph vague and weak.\r\n\r\nStrong writing nonetheless! Keep it up!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 11:59:18','2025-10-07 11:59:18'),(19554,'judge-event-evaluation-25242-1759802480',25242,439,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,7053,4679,8535,11,NULL,NULL,100,89.00,NULL,NULL,'',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 12:01:20','2025-10-07 12:01:20'),(19555,'judge-event-evaluation-24959-1759802604',24959,439,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,7047,4679,8535,11,NULL,NULL,100,83.00,NULL,NULL,'',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 12:03:24','2025-10-07 12:03:24'),(19556,'judge-event-evaluation-27638-1759802725',27638,429,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,7500,394,8535,11,NULL,NULL,100,77.00,NULL,NULL,'',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 12:05:25','2025-10-07 12:05:25'),(19557,'judge-event-evaluation-24561-1759813785',24561,430,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,7619,392,NULL,5,NULL,NULL,100,78.00,-10,-2.00,'Hi Metra,\r\nGreat work on engaging writing on such a relevant topic in this day and age - a fascinating read!\r\n\r\nYou writing skills are quite strong, but sadly you haven\'t written to the format you are competing for. As I read through the essay, I think you\'ve unintentionally missed the point of a persuasive essay. You have instead written a compelling case study on mental health, comparing unnoticed or overboard. You\'ve spent most of your word count focusing on the current climate, addressing the tensions between the two extremes very well. However, I only understood the direction of your persuasion at the conclusion. You should have stated a topic towards one side of an argument from the beginning, and then used the comparison studies and the tensions as emphasis of WHY the direction you are persuading is the right way to go.\r\n\r\nYou have a strong title, but your essay has not clearly stated the thesis statement. The title should play the role of a hook, being short and sweet summary of your topic. But it\'s role is not to state the thesis statement. Your sentence: \"That’s the dilemma: awareness exists, yet empathy in practice still lags behind.\" could\'ve been the part where you stated the thesis statement as it seems like you\'re suggesting a persuasion towards building empathy in practice around mental health. But the way it\'s written is that you\'re focused on the dilemma between awareness and false empathy. Next time, start with something like, \"Therefore..\" then you state what you are persuading the reader towards (in this case, perhaps the need for empathy in practice to be improved and normalised in schools.).\r\n\r\nYou have a strong narrative style of writing, which works very well for your examples and real-life scenarios. This seems to be your strength, however there are occasions when your writing tone becomes too conversational for the format of a persuasive essay. An example is: \"Disorders get turned into meme formats.\" In writing, it should be something along the lines of: \"Disorders become/are turned into meme formats.\" My challenge for you is to go through all the \"get\" and \"got\" and replace them with more intentional words. That will add more depth and character to your points.\r\n\r\nI also would suggest to be intentional with your voice. When it doesn\'t need to be \'casual\' in an essay, don\'t make it to be as it detracts from the weight of your argument. You still need to maintain a consistent voice throughout, but use your narrative style as a tool. Formal language hold weight, while casual, narrative style brings relevance and emotion. Here\'s a few phrases where you\'ve done well: \" ...and people begin to treat them as funny traits rather than serious struggles. Disorders become hashtags, symptoms become punchlines...\"\r\n\r\nIn terms of writing fundamentals, it\'s important that you work on how you determine paragraphs. Currently, your essay reads as if your paragraph breaks are for when a breath needs to be taken. This may work in story writing, but an essay need to have its paragraphs divided based on central ideas. 1 strong key point per paragraph written in the opening sentence, then the body supports the point, then the last sentence of that paragraph has a strong closing statement that justify why your point is valid. \r\n\r\nLastly, one point deducted as an essay traditionally shouldn\'t have the headings included, it should only have a title and body. The beginning of each paragraph should also be indented. Another point deducted as word count is not stated.\r\n\r\nYou seriously have a strong writing voice, and I encourage you to continue to explore it. A good writer will learn how to adapt to different formats :)\r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 15:09:45','2025-10-07 15:09:45'),(19560,'judge-event-evaluation-24561-1759814780',24561,430,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,7619,392,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,79.00,-10,-2.00,'Hi Metra,\r\nGreat work at writing such an engaging piece on a topic that\'s so incredibly personal yet largely relevant to many! You have a strong writing voice that\'s easy to read and follow. \r\n\r\nAs I read through your essay, I think you have unintentionally missed the writing format of the persuasive essay. This paper reads more like a case study that compares the extremes of mental health awareness. You spent a lot of your word count in addressing the current climate and the tensions, which you have done incredibly well. However, the emphasis is heavier on that than trying to persuade the reader towards one direction. \r\n\r\nTo follow on the above, you also have not clearly stated the thesis statement. Your title seem to suggest to it, but it\'s would\'ve been better stated in your introduction paragraph. It seems like this could\'ve been your thesis statement: \"That’s the dilemma: awareness exists, yet empathy in practice still lags behind.\" However, the choice of word \"dilemma\" and the paragraphs that follow was again focused on the tension. In the future, start with \"Therefore,\" then state which direction you are aiming to persuade (in your case, perhaps it\'s the urgent need for empathy in practice to be improved in schools.)\r\n\r\nYou also have a very strong narrative style, which seems to work well in your examples! However, I did find that sometimes your writing comes across too conversational for the formal of an essay. An easy example is your frequent use of the word \'get/got\': \"Disorders get turned into meme formats.\" I challenge you to replace all the gets and gots to more intentional words, and that will help in adding weight and character to your writing.\r\n\r\nSimilarly, be intentional on your writing voice to maximise impact. For a persuasive essay, more formal language gives depth and authority in your reasoning, while casual words add relevance and emotion. Use them as tools while maintaining consistency. Here\'s an example of where you used casual writing to create great character and impact: \"...and people begin to treat them as funny traits rather than serious struggles. Disorders become hashtags, symptoms become punchlines,...\"\r\n\r\nLastly, 2 deductions as a traditional essay should not have the headings included (only a title and paragraphs), and you have not submitted the word count.\r\n\r\nI can see your writing style coming through, and I encourage you to keep growing at it! A great writer will learn how to write for different formats :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 15:26:20','2025-10-07 15:26:20'),(19564,'judge-event-evaluation-26596-1759817736',26596,463,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,9112,5934,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,69.00,-10,-5.00,'Hi Kevin,\r\nGreat attempt at this essay. Your points are incredibly clear and logical, easy to follow and read. \r\n\r\nYour outline is written with create consistency in the sentence structure. However, an outline should not include a hook, key verse, thesis statement and final thought. Neither these elements nor full, long sentences should be a part of the outline. These things should be listed in the essay itself. \r\n\r\nWhile the key points you made are logically relevant, your opening & closing paragraphs and the formatting do not support a persuasive essay writing style. The way this topic is written comes across as more of a preaching monologue, rather than a persuasive essay. The 1st paragraph should state your thesis statement clearly, then your last paragraph summarises all your points in the middle paragraphs and closes with a strong statement. You also shouldn\'t be finishing your essay with a question, as it doesn\'t support attempt of persuading the reader. In terms of formatting, every paragraph should start indented, and there shouldn\'t be double/triple spacing between paragraphs. \r\n\r\nOn the other hand, the middle paragraphs (where you numbered) are delivered well. It would\'ve have been better if they were slightly longer as they would have been more persuasive, but the structure and writing works.\r\n\r\nPoints deducted as word count not stated, and the essay needs to be on plain white background, as clearly stated in the judges form.\r\n\r\nGreat work, and I would challenge you to apply your strengths into more relevant topics for a persuasive essay format!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 16:15:36','2025-10-07 16:15:36'),(19565,'judge-event-evaluation-26351-1759818347',26351,433,21,7,3,2025,349,'767','1',0,5317,9290,30,NULL,NULL,100,54.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Keren, thank you for submitting your instrumental composition.\r\n\r\nMusically, it was difficult to fully understand what was going on during your song. The violin melody was missing from the audio recording that was uploaded, and therefore the melody was marked down. \r\nWhen writing for piano, especially with a rich synthesised sound, make sure to space your voicing out from a closed position to an open position. Most of the chords were muddy in sound because of the choice of voicing combined with the texture of the synth sound. Opening up the voicing, changing the sound, or even simply playing in a higher register will help it sound less muddy and give it more clarity.\r\nThe bass line is technically fine, but a simple way to make things sound better is to line up the bass notes with the kick drum. This will help make the whole song feel cohesive. Use the repeated notes when you want to build, and use both the kick drum and the bass together to increase the intensity of the song rhythmically. You already have the guitar and the marimba playing a lot rhythmically, so you don\'t also need the bass to follow that as it can become too much. \r\nThe chord progression was not clear from bars 37 onwards until about bar 45, because your piano chords and the bass were clashing. If you are using extensions to chords, such as suspended chords or 7th chords, make sure that they are spaced in nicer voicings, otherwise it will become muddy and unclear as to what the chord is meant to be.\r\n\r\nReadability wise, try and keep your lines to 4 bars or 8 bars when you format it so that it is easy to follow.\r\n\r\nYou submitted a midi file - which meant there was no performance applicable.\r\n\r\nThe audio file and the music sheet did not match up - the violin seemed to be missing entirely or altered from the original sheet music.\r\n\r\nThank you again for your submission, and I hope that the feedback will help you improve on future submissions.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 16:25:47','2025-10-07 16:25:47'),(19568,'judge-event-evaluation-25897-1759819875',25897,430,21,7,3,2025,349,'767','1',0,392,9290,30,NULL,NULL,100,75.00,NULL,NULL,'Well done Kevin. This is a nice piece that you have composed.\r\n\r\nMusically, this is a well written piece. Objectively, there is nothing wrong with the piece, yet there is room for improvement.\r\nMelodically, from bars 88 to 112, the violin and piano are both playing separate melodies. This makes it confusing as to what the listener needs to pay attention to as the melody. It would\'ve been nice if the melody was removed from the piano at that point, to allow some space for the violin to take a more lead role instead of a supporting role. Sharing melodies around different instruments also creates interesting and diverse expressions of the same melody. With the three stringed instruments and the flute, there definitely is space to be desired for them to take the melody at different points to allow for those different expressions. \r\nHarmonically, the same is true. The piano is a prominent part of the harmony but because it is playing chords in its left hand all the time, it doesn\'t allow space for the other instruments to really take part in the harmony. Again, with a string instrument and the flute, utilise long legato chords, as this is something the piano is unable to do, and let the piano take a break from playing chords on every beat. Make the voicing of the left hand in the piano a bit more sparse to allow other instruments to fill that harmonic space. \r\nRhythmically, the driving force of the song is good, but it is intense. Bar 179 is a very welcome addition to the song, however because of how intense this song is, it probably needed a lighter and slower part like this much earlier in the song to provide more contrast. \r\nOverall, the song is good, but the intensity in melody, harmony, and rhythm, all add up for it to be too much without loosening up on some of the parts. Give the song some more variation in all of these, and it will become a much more holistic listening experience.\r\n\r\nWhilst you can write the song in 3/4, it is definitely a 6/8 song. The difference between 3/4 is that you have 3 downbeats in 3/4, but you have 2 downbeats in 6/8.\r\n\r\nFor readability, format the song so that the next line is every 4 or 8 bars wherever possible.\r\n\r\nThe song is not too difficult - but at the end, some of the flute and piano arpeggios are very difficult and would not be easily played.\r\n\r\nI have deducted a point for ministry because the intensity of the song can be overwhelming.\r\n\r\nThe performance was a midi performance, and so you received 0 for IVA and IVB. \r\n\r\nOverall, well done.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 16:51:15','2025-10-07 16:51:15'),(19570,'judge-event-evaluation-23888-1759820911',23888,447,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,7078,6328,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,64.00,-10,-8.00,'Hi Mischa,\r\nYou\'ve chosen a very interesting topic, and great to see you\'ve used a lot of Scriptural examples to strengthen your point. \r\n\r\nIn the future, I would suggest refraining from ending your paragraphs with Scriptural quotes. While using Scriptural references are a great way to support your argument, it should not be the main writer of your essay. For the format of a persuasive essay, your last sentence in each paragraph should be a strong closing statement that summarises the point of that paragraph written by you. \r\n\r\nUnfortunately, you have gone over the word count significantly -- it needs to be a maximum of 1000 as stated in this judges form. While having 6 examples (3 failures and 3 successes) demonstrated that you have researched your topic, the quantity has not increased the validity and persuasion of your argument - 2 each would have been enough and helped kept you within the word limit.\r\n\r\nYour outline is well organised; the phrasings are short, sweet and clear. In terms of structure, my feedback to you is to work on the consistency of the sentence structure. Heading II and its subheadings do not align with the phrasings of the other headings.  However, it terms of its effectiveness, it could be strengthen. The bulk of your essay uses examples to structure the flow. While I would suggest framing it around the point you\'re trying to make and then using those examples to strengthen. Eg: Your point could be: \"Putting faith in the Lord may result in great assignment,\" and then you use Elisha to support it. \r\n\r\nI did find that while your outline is clearly written, the essay does not follow the same amount of clarity. I often had to read back to the outline to understand your intention of another example -- this should not be the case. From the opening line of each paragraph, I should be able to get an idea of the purpose of the new paragraph, as it should have a clear point. \r\n\r\nI can see you have a strong line of thinking of how you can research and strongly support a topic, and I would encourage you to work on your fundamental essay writing skills so you can deliver this better :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 17:08:31','2025-10-07 17:08:31'),(19574,'judge-event-evaluation-26601-1759823320',26601,463,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,8115,5934,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,85.00,-10,-2.00,'Hi Nathalie,\r\n\r\nStrong delivery of this topic, with many essential points covered. \r\n\r\nYour outline is impressive; it\'s well structured, consistently phrased, easy to follow and gives a great overview of your plan and flow. However, the outline should not include the titles \"hook\", \"thesis statement\", \"Repeat thesis statement\" and \"suggestion\". These are tools of what can be used in your essay, but does not fit the structure of the outline. Your outline should just cover the high level points you are going to unpack.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately I felt like your paragraphs do not progress as clearly as your outline has. You\'ve used your subpoints as your opening sentence of a paragraph. I can see that your paragraphs have a similar flow order to your outline, but by reading the essay itself, it does not clearly direct the structure. What a good persuasive essay structure should look like is that the beginning of each paragraph should state the point you are making, then the body of the essay should have supporting points (just like you did in the outline), and then the end of each paragraph has a closing statement that justifies and further persuades the reader. Your writing style is more towards a preaching topic rather than a persuasive essay in written form. \r\n\r\nDeduction as word count not included.\r\n\r\nNonetheless, great attempt at this topic. Your outline skills give you great foundation to be able to guide future writing. Keep it up :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 17:48:40','2025-10-07 17:48:40'),(19577,'judge-event-evaluation-26252-1759830503',26252,446,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,7973,2276,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,88.00,-10,-2.00,'Hi Stephanie,\r\n\r\nWell done on a excellent persuasive essay! Your writing is clear and precise, your points in their paragraphs flow logically. The outline is thoughtfully crafted, and is well reflected in the essay. Your writing style is easy to read, with great pacing and varied sentences. There\'s consistency in your style, but also thoughtfully varied between using complex technical language and emotionally persuasive wording.\r\n\r\nIt is highly unfortunate that you have not included a bibliography. This is essential to your essay as you referenced studies, statistics and numbers that you would have had to have taken from another source. You have also not included the word count, which resulted in further deduction. \r\n\r\nSo in the future, I\'d strongly recommend reading the guidelines before finalising your submission to ensure that you include everything required -- you want your submission to reflect your excellence well! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 19:48:23','2025-10-07 19:48:23'),(19578,'judge-event-evaluation-26871-1759831851',26871,464,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,8175,1009,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,62.00,-10,-2.00,'Hi Valerio, \r\nYou have picked a topic with high potential and relevance. However it is unfortunate that your writing was not structured in a way that fits a persuasive essay. Your suggested the topic in your title, but it is not clearly stated in the first paragraph of what you are aiming to persuade. In fact, the persuasion towards a direction of the topic of AI seem to only start in the last paragraph. The middle paragraphs are studies into AI, however they still do not reason to convince and support a direction of a point. \r\n\r\nPoints deducted as word count is not stated.\r\n\r\nI encourage that you learn the fundamentals of essay writing: start your essay by stating the intention of what you\'re persuading as your topic, then identify 3-4 points that support your topic (under each paragraph is where you can spell out the details, history, pros and cons, and whatever you find can be useful), and then end the paragraph with a strong summary of why your points justify your direction of persuasion.\r\n\r\nAll the best.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 20:10:51','2025-10-07 20:10:51'),(19579,'judge-event-evaluation-24560-1759831932',24560,430,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,7621,392,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,87.00,-10,-2.00,'Hi Michelle,\r\n\r\nVery strong essay: it\'s clear, well supported with Scripture, and focused. I would like to see a little more real life examples or illustrations as that would have made it more persuasive than just stating facts (Scripture). The Scriptures are used to support and justify your writing, but it shouldn\'t be the bulk of your persuasion in this essay.\r\n\r\nTo improve your outline structure, I\'d recommend working on the consistency of the phrasing. While quoting Scriptural references are important, they do not tell the reader what the context is (in some you have a phrase next to it, in others you don\'t). It\'s best if you let the outlines just have phrases or short sentences that summarises the high level of your points, and then reference the Scripture in the essay itself.\r\n\r\nYour writing is consistent and clear, however, it\'s unfortunate that there are many punctuation mistakes: double spacings, extra spaces before and after commas, double spacing after a paragraph that doesn\'t need it. Please proof read as this could\'ve been easily avoided. Deduction also because word count is not stated.\r\n\r\nStill great writing! I would encourage you to explore writing beyond a Scriptural sermon -- this can help strengthen your writing voice and style :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 20:12:12','2025-10-07 20:12:12'),(19580,'judge-event-evaluation-26599-1759832032',26599,463,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,8144,5934,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,86.00,-10,0.00,'Your writing is strong, clear and uses a large vocabulary. Your key points are well thought out and carefully crafted. \r\n\r\nHowever, the progression of your ideas can be improved. For the structure of a persuasive essay, your sentences should not start with a reference or Scripture, as it should state your key point. References and Scripture should support and back up your point. Similarly, the ending of each sentence should summarise your point, and using the body of your paragraph to justify your reasoning. Currently, your paragraphs flow, but it does not clearly breakdown where an essential point of argument starts and stops. \r\n\r\nI also notice inconsistencies in the quality of your essay to your outline. Your language in the outline is much simpler, your phrasing is inconsistent and not as refined and complex as your essay. I am hesitant to believe that your essay has not received other external assistance, whether digitally or a collaborative effort. \r\n\r\nNonetheless, great attempt at an essay with precise word choices. ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 20:13:52','2025-10-07 20:13:52'),(19581,'judge-event-evaluation-25306-1759832726',25306,458,21,7,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7420,4200,9289,6,'Collection',NULL,100,60.00,-10,0.00,'Hi Angellina,\r\n\r\nGreat attempt of emotion used in this poem!\r\n\r\nSadly it is unclear who the voice is. For a topic with such intense emotion and phrasings that mimic conversation, it\'s important that the reader can identify who is speaking. \r\n\r\nI can see you using some form of pattern of rhythm in some of the stanzas, but there is no consistency or intentionality of the changing of the rhythm or form.\r\n\r\nLearning basic poetry structures may help you to better express what you\'re trying to convey!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 20:25:26','2025-10-07 20:25:26'),(19585,'judge-event-evaluation-25959-1759835558',25959,463,21,7,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,8097,5934,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,89.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Ellyz,\r\n\r\nWell done on a fresh narrative of the life of Jesus! I like your use of imagery that has natural and still-relevant occurrence to describe how human He was, including the cry for milk and the path of mud. The walk in the market with His mum used to compare His relationship with the Father is also clever and beautiful. \r\n\r\nFor improvement, I would suggest being more intentional about the number of feet per line, and making sure they are consistent. If you are wanting to have variety, be intentionally clear. Your choice of poetry style is one quite traditional, therefore it is important that you keep to the traditional measures. You have done well in keeping the rhyme traditional, but the pacing and rhythm could be better.\r\n\r\nI would also suggest capitalising nouns and pronouns referring to God, so that includes \"He\", \"Father\", \"Him/His\".\r\n\r\nOtherwise, beautiful piece and I encourage you to keep writing!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 21:12:38','2025-10-07 21:12:38'),(19587,'judge-event-evaluation-25240-1759836367',25240,439,21,7,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,9011,4679,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,89.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Gishella,\r\n\r\nBeautiful simple piece about your relationship with Jesus!\r\n\r\nI love your use of simple words. It creates a consistent and clear voice, and impactful in the way that the poem is written. However, I do think you could use more fresh phrases that are not commonly heard or used. Think about if there are other ways to describe your point!\r\n\r\nStrong start into poetry writing, and I encourage you to keep writing!\r\n\r\nI would also recommend checking that all pronouns referring to God are capitalised. ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 21:26:07','2025-10-07 21:26:07'),(19602,'judge-event-evaluation-24983-1759845342',24983,464,21,7,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,8186,1009,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,97.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Russel, \r\nIncredible poem! You\'ve taken a modern style of poetry, and executed it very well. It\'s intentionally delivered without feeling forceful. I can see influences of the book of Psalms in the wrathful style of writing while still keeping your eyes on the Lord. \r\n\r\nThe pacing is consistent, and phrasing strong. The word choice are deliberate, and rolls of the tongue very smoothly. There are some witty and clever word & phrasing play including \"There was never justice, just people.\" and breaking the word \"here\" in the next line. You\'ve used pacing very effectively. \r\n\r\nI do find that some of your analogies are slightly lost, such as the use of colour. Considering your tone is very direct and sharp, the use of olden language (including behold and strife) feels like it weakens the point and breaks character rather than sharpen. Also deduction for not having double spacing format as stated in the student convention guidelines.\r\n\r\nStill, overall very well executed especially for your age. You have a knack for the craft and I hope you continue to write!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 23:55:42','2025-10-07 23:55:42'),(19603,'judge-event-evaluation-25610-1759845415',25610,446,21,7,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,9060,2276,9289,6,'Collection',NULL,100,84.00,-10,0.00,'Hi Annabelle,\r\n\r\nWell done on a concise, strong poem!\r\n\r\nYou\'ve used the rhythm well, incredibly consistent phrasing throughout without repetition. While the writing is strong, I would\'ve liked to see more original phrases used rather than commonly used Christian phrasing. Also deduction for not having double spacing format as stated in the student convention guidelines.\r\n\r\nYou have a good grasp on the fundamentals of poetry, and I encourage you to continue writing!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 23:56:55','2025-10-07 23:56:55'),(19604,'judge-event-evaluation-27565-1759845520',27565,435,21,7,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,9200,1763,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,90.00,-10,-3.00,'Hi Ghijkl,\r\n\r\nSuch a beautiful rendition of a wonderful psalm! Your pacing is consistent, and phrasing effectively used. Very intentional use of commas to break pace and suggest rhythm. \r\n\r\nWhile the word \"rife\" has multiple meanings, I do think it tends to have a stronger negative connotation. Therefore it has not played as well of an impact in the piece as you\'d hoped. I would also like to see more original phrasings put together. \r\n\r\nWhile I commend your creativity, you have marks deducted as the judges form clearly states that the submission must be on plain white paper. Also a deduction for not having double spacing format as stated in the student convention guidelines.\r\n\r\nA beautiful piece - nonetheless!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-07 23:58:40','2025-10-07 23:58:40'),(19605,'judge-event-evaluation-26369-1759845673',26369,433,21,7,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,8975,5317,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,95.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Jillian,\r\n\r\nVery powerful piece! I love your use of imagery, describing tangible experiences of their travel journey alongside their faith journey.\r\n\r\nI would suggest avoiding repeating the same word multiple times (\"through\" has been used 3x, including 2x in one line). To also improve your flow and meter, consider how stress and unstressed syllables work together. Do they roll of the tongue well after each other? Are there a lot of consonants to closely together, even though there is the same number of feet in each line?\r\n\r\nOne deduction for not having double spacing format as stated in the student convention guidelines.\r\n\r\nWell done! You have a knack at this and I encourage you to keep writing!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 00:01:13','2025-10-08 00:01:13'),(19606,'judge-event-evaluation-23887-1759845693',23887,447,21,7,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7074,6328,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,94.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Joaquine,\r\n\r\nThis is such a fresh perspective of a common topic - great delivery!\r\n\r\nYour choice of imagery and description is refreshing, 10/10 for originality. However, I did mark down as you used the same words multiple times, but not in the most intentional way. An example is that \"Searched\" has been used 3x; the last two can be seen as intentional to impress upon the pursuit, but then the first one should\'ve been changed to another word to ensure the emphasis of the last two hits home. \r\n\r\nI would also try to keep the consistency of the meter, unless you can clearly demonstrate intention choice of breaking. Stanza 3 felt like it broke the flow of the rhythm.\r\n\r\nOne deduction for not having double spacing format as stated in the student convention guidelines.\r\n\r\nVery great effort, and I would encourage you to keep writing - it\'s refreshing and I hope it blessed the other readers too!\r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 00:01:33','2025-10-08 00:01:33'),(19607,'judge-event-evaluation-24960-1759845746',24960,439,21,7,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7047,4679,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,88.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Keisha,\r\n\r\nGreat job! This poem takes a simple topic and delivered with consistent phrasing and voicing. Your rhyming is also strong.\r\n\r\nThe title is beautiful, and cleverly used as the ending of the poem. Considering the use of imagery of the word \"stream\", it would\'ve been nice to see you embody the word stream in a creative way. This can look like using more \'stream\'-related words (I noticed you used the word ocean, which is a good start. But a couple would\'ve been better to tie in with the theme). Another way can be in the choice of words and how they sound when read... does it flow like a stream of water? Does it feel like and easy? Are there a lot of s\'s used to sound like water running?\r\n\r\nDeduction for not having double spacing format as stated in the student convention guidelines.\r\n\r\nGreat start, and I encourage you to keep writing!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 00:02:26','2025-10-08 00:02:26'),(19608,'judge-event-evaluation-25796-1759845804',25796,433,21,7,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,8001,5317,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,78.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Kenneth,\r\n\r\nGreat work on narrating the journey of the man and the shepherd. The simplicity of the words you chose in the first half of the poem read off like a trotting of the horse\'s journey, which comes across nicely. \r\n\r\nI would suggest working on your rhythm and consistency of rhyme. Some stanzas have clear pairings of the rhymes, other do not and break pattern without clear intention. I would also consider counting the  feet in each meter to ensure it matches up -- unless you are deliberately breaking it, which in this case would require you to demonstrate a new pattern somehow. Either way, this is not evident in the poem. \r\n\r\nAlso deduction for not having double spacing format as stated in the student convention guidelines.\r\n\r\nAgain, great work and keep at it!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 00:03:24','2025-10-08 00:03:24'),(19609,'judge-event-evaluation-26000-1759845861',26000,463,21,7,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,9082,5934,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,77.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Richelle,\r\nGreat attempt at a classic topic. I like your use of simple language to match a simple title. I can see your uses of rhyme as best as you can.\r\n\r\nHowever, the repetitive use of words reduces the impact and creativity of the piece. An example is that \"How\" is used 3x in the first three sentences and \"is\" is used 2x, but they do not match up in pattern on intentionality. If your intent is to use the \"How ____ is\" phrasing for impact, then you should\'ve avoided using \"how\" in the third line. \"All\" is better used in the 4th stanza, but then \"give us\" is repeated again in the middle of stanza 5. If your intention is to use the repeated use of words (in stanza 1, 4 and 5) as a poetic device, then  raises the question, \"Where is the pattern?\"\r\n\r\nAlso deduction for not having double spacing format as stated in the student convention guidelines.\r\n\r\nI hope this helps, and encourages you to think creatively!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 00:04:21','2025-10-08 00:04:21'),(19610,'judge-event-evaluation-26031-1759845926',26031,463,21,7,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,8096,5934,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,93.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Theodora,\r\n\r\nCreative play from the inspiration of Edelweiss! I can see your clever use of poetic devices in your writing, using symbolism of the flowers throughout in different ways.\r\n\r\nI love the deliberately broken phrasing of long and short variants in the first two stanzas. However, I found the transition from stanza 2 to 3 abrupt as it suddenly changes to consistent meter and rhyme, but without clear pattern or reason to why it happened. Then in stanza 5 onwards, it returns back to the your version of the Edelweiss format. Your writing style is strong with much character, so I wished stanza 2 & 3 maintained your own structure and voice than reverting to traditional form. \r\n\r\nAlso a deduction for not having double spacing format as stated in the student convention guidelines.\r\n\r\nI encourage you to continue on the curiousity of merging themes and exploring new voicings! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 00:05:26','2025-10-08 00:05:26'),(19611,'judge-event-evaluation-23999-1759845959',23999,447,21,7,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7083,6328,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,87.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Valerie,\r\nBeautiful poem on your hope in Jesus. I can see Scriptural references weaved in beautifully throughout. The pacing is consistent and effective.\r\n\r\nConsidering this is a classic topic, I would suggest exploring how you can convey it in newer, more original ways. A lot of the phrasings you chose, while they are relevant and well rhymed, are commonly used. Examples include, \"pure and clean,\" \"The storm may rage,\" and the opening \"When shadows fall and nights grow long.\" The opening line sets the tone of your style, and I encourage that is should be more unique to your voice.\r\n\r\nAlso deduction for not having double spacing format as stated in the student convention guidelines.\r\n\r\nGreat work and keep writing!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 00:05:59','2025-10-08 00:05:59'),(19612,'judge-event-evaluation-26014-1759846023',26014,463,21,7,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,8098,5934,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,91.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Yohana,\r\nCreative use of imagery across this poem. Your choice of words describe the story very tangibly, like a narrative piece should.\r\n\r\nHowever, I do think there are repetitive use of words that missed demonstrating its intentionality. With the exception of \"He walked, walked every step like a vow,\" repeating words so closely together dulls the impact. You have \'touch\' twice in the first stanza to rhyme with itself, and then \"deserve\" is repeated 3 times, but the tense changed unclearly.\r\n\r\nI noticed you only had one 3-line stanza, but can\'t see why doing so made the delivery more effective. I think if you were going to do so, the writing must be more obvious or repeat the 3-line stanza further below for a pattern. This would\'ve provided another layer of intentionality, which in this case is left for question. \r\n\r\nAlso deduction for not having double spacing format as stated in the student convention guidelines.\r\n\r\nStill, a great job at painting such a monumental picture!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 00:07:03','2025-10-08 00:07:03'),(19613,'judge-event-evaluation-24544-1759846084',24544,430,21,7,3,2025,6,'012',NULL,7596,392,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,96.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Christopher,\r\nExcellent poem! Your writing flows very smoothly with a strong, yet fresh narrative. There\'s a nice song-like rhythm in your piece, with beautiful natural balance of consonants and vowels that flow off the tongue.  \r\n\r\nMy favourite is the closing line, so beautifully put. Well done. Considering it\'s such a powerful ending with the word \"love\", it could be even better if the word \"love\" was not already used before. For future writing, I\'d encourage you to consider how your phrasings can be more original, even if you\'re trying to convey a topic so classic.\r\n\r\nA deduction for not having double spacing format as stated in the student convention guidelines.\r\n\r\nKeep writing, you have a knack for it!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 00:08:04','2025-10-08 00:08:04'),(19615,'judge-event-evaluation-24559-1759847808',24559,430,21,7,3,2025,19,'061',NULL,7617,392,9289,5,NULL,NULL,100,87.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Kevin,\r\nGreat effort on tackling such a big topic! Emotional intelligence can be very nuanced, and you did a good job on identifying the key points that to cover within the limited word count you have. Here are few points of improvement that I hope you can take for your future writing.\r\n\r\nYour opening sentence could be stronger, as it doesn\'t give me the urgency of why it\'s talked about (I\'d argue many things today are talked about... like wagyu beef, travel plans, or Labubus... then what makes emotional intelligence worth writing about?). The first sentence to an essay needs to capture the reader\'s attention, establish the general topic, and set the tone for the paper by drawing the reader into the introduction and preparing them for the essay\'s argument. While you title suggests the theme, it would\'ve been better if you had one strong sentence at the end of your first paragraph that states what your key point of argument/discussion is.\r\n\r\nYour second sentence was going strong with great examples, however from your sentence \"Christians could also claim...\" that starts going on a tangent that doesn\'t support the main point of your paragraph. If you think that was worth writing about, then it should\'ve been in a separate paragraph. The closing statement for that paragraph also then does not support the opening sentence, which weakens the persuasion of the paragraph. The opening of every paragraph should introduce 1 point and then close with a stronger closing statement to emphasis it; the sentences in between should all support that 1 point. So after you write the opening sentence, you should be thinking \"do all these sentences that follow in this paragraph strongly support it? if not then it does not belong in this paragraph.\"\r\n\r\nSimilar to your closing sentence, it\'s important that you do not start a paragraph with a reference or quote. The closing paragraph should strongly state WHY your argument is correct and worth agreeing to. Then you use the body of your last paragraph to restate (even stronger) the reasons that support your argument. \r\n\r\nLastly is some feedback on word choice. You\'ve used the word stupid a few times; while the sure may be relevant as the opposite of intelligence, but you used it in the context to describe intelligence. So that has not helped the reader measure what the lack of emotional intelligence look like. A better way is to describe what the traits are. I would also refrain from using phrases like \"...as simple as it gets.\" Don\'t tell the reader it\'s simple, show it, write about it. By using phrases like that, you\'re assuming it\'s simple for the reader. Your role of the writer is to simplify it by writing clearly and simply. \r\n\r\nWell done, and all the best for your future writing. ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 00:36:48','2025-10-08 00:36:48'),(19616,'judge-event-evaluation-26537-1759849405',26537,461,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,8303,7991,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,81.00,-10,NULL,'',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 01:03:25','2025-10-08 01:03:25'),(19621,'judge-event-evaluation-26179-1759853017',26179,463,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,8129,5934,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,0.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Feivel,\r\n\r\nGreat pacing, and strong rhyme. You\'ve used the meter effectively while clearly delivering your message.\r\n\r\nI would encourage you to explore more original phrases and get creative with the exploring poetic devices. This will help bring character and voice to your writing style.\r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 02:03:37','2025-10-17 03:42:33'),(19623,'judge-event-evaluation-25769-1759853351',25769,429,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,7088,394,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,78.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Clara,\r\n\r\nGreat attempt at having a clear poetic form and structure. You\'ve used the rhyming well. \r\n\r\nHowever, I would encourage you to explore more original ways to express your idea. A lot of your phrasing are commonly used and cliche, such as \"In a world so big and wide\" and \"Shine your light through darkest days.\" \r\n\r\nDeduction as well for the lack of double spacing format as stated in the student convention guidelines. ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 02:09:11','2025-10-08 02:09:11'),(19624,'judge-event-evaluation-25538-1759853571',25538,429,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,7085,394,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,83.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Cheryl,\r\n\r\nThere is strong imagery used to describe light in various contexts, as consistent with your theme.\r\n\r\nHowever, I would consider exploring more original ways to express your point, as some phrasings are commonly used in poetry and cliche. Examples include:  \"light within your soul\" and \'For light will guide, and light will show.\" While your topic is light, it is part of the process to think outside of the box beyond the physical form of light and the Scriptural representation of light.\r\n\r\nPoint also deducted for not having the double spacing format as stated in the SC guidelines.\r\n\r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 02:12:51','2025-10-08 02:12:51'),(19625,'judge-event-evaluation-26277-1759893404',26277,463,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,8158,5934,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,93.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Felicia,\r\n\r\nGreat poem! The pacing, rhyme and meter is very smooth, effective and flows nicely of the tongue. The word choices nice creates a consistent voice that matches the title. There\'s a great balance about the story of Jesus while using imagery and illustration to add emphasis and emotion.\r\n\r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 13:16:44','2025-10-08 13:16:44'),(19629,'judge-event-evaluation-25251-1759894349',25251,439,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,7042,4679,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,64.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Keithanno,\r\n\r\nThank you for a beautiful poem. It points to the Lord and should bless all who read it.\r\n\r\nI would encourage you to expand the piece further by exploring more original phrasings and rhyme. I can see your inspiration from Isaiah 41:10, which is a good start. But a great poem looks at ways to communicate the same message in new creative ways. \r\n\r\nA point deduction as this should have been formatted in double spacing as written in the SC guidelines.\r\n\r\nKeep at it, and all the best!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 13:32:29','2025-10-08 13:32:29'),(19630,'judge-event-evaluation-25541-1759894383',25541,429,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,7089,394,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,64.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Clarissa,\r\n\r\nYour poem is short and sweet, using the meter correctly. However it does lack character and originality. I would encourage you to explore creative ways of how to expand the idea.\r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 13:33:03','2025-10-08 13:33:03'),(19631,'judge-event-evaluation-25308-1759896925',25308,458,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,9220,4200,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,97.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Jesse,\r\n\r\nThis is so beautifully original. Your voice is strong, and style consistent. Simple yet grounded. \r\nYour meter and rhyme is intentional. There is a clear pattern of the repetition if \"I walk; I walked; I fell.\" The uses of repetition is effective and does not feel as an accident. I would consider that that the first stanza should\'ve been in past tense, however it was present tense consistently for the whole 1st stanza, so that might\'ve been intentional.\r\n\r\nThe only point deducted is that it should\'ve been in double spacing as written in the SC guidelines.\r\n\r\nThank you -- Your poem has blessed my heart today. I\'m moved and encouraged with the perseverance to continue on when times get tough. Well done. May you bless others with your skills and keep pressing on in the Lord. ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 14:15:25','2025-10-08 14:15:25'),(19632,'judge-event-evaluation-24563-1759897771',24563,430,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,7617,392,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,0.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Kevin,\r\nWhat a beautiful, original poem! Your writing voice is strong and clear, with urgency and clear articulation. You use imagery well, especially how you use contrasting as a tool to paint the image of war by juxtaposing it against more gentler, precious things in life (roses, sheep, and even age).\r\n\r\nYour rhythm is strong, almost like a march -- first two lines of stanza 4 has so much character!\r\nI did notice your tense in the first line should be past tense (\"were\" killed). Sheep is both singular and plural, so sheeps is wrong (stanza 4).\r\n\r\nFor improvement, I would also try to remove filler words & phrases, phrases like \"looking like\" in stanza 4. I challenge you to consider how you can sharpen the words and be more concise; ask yourself if there are any words that can better describe it. In this example, perhaps \"looking like they\'re in\" can be replace with \"appear\". You can also do this with verbs, asking yourself how can replace a word that describes an action with another word that adds more character while still portraying the action? An example would be for the line: \"...as their fiery death approached near.\" Can you replace \"approached\" with something else? Maybe \"marched\" \"creeped\" or \"seeped\"? These words give the noun \"fiery death\" more character like it\'s a person.\r\n\r\nWell done. I was moved and impressed with how much of you I can read through this poem. You have a knack with this and I encourage you to keep writing!!!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 14:29:31','2025-10-17 02:39:13'),(19633,'judge-event-evaluation-25309-1759900043',25309,458,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,9234,4200,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,84.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Lygia,\r\n\r\nBeautiful gentle poem about God\'s love!\r\n\r\nYour pacing and rhyme is consistent, with a nice rhythm throughout.\r\n\r\nI would love to see more creative flair in the descriptions, thinking outside of the box. You\'ve used \'shadows\' twice to describe challenges. The link between the weather elements (light, storm, shadow) as challenges and the shelter as God\'s protection is great, but I would\'ve liked to see more imagery of the shelter. Descriptors would\'ve been nice to paint a picture. \r\n\r\nAlso deduction as the poem needs to be in double spacing as written in the SC guidelines. \r\n\r\nWell done and keep improving!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 15:07:23','2025-10-08 15:07:23'),(19634,'judge-event-evaluation-25241-1759901132',25241,439,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,7041,4679,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,72.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Matthew,\r\n\r\nGreat attempt at writing about hope! \r\n\r\nI would encourage you to use different words throughout your poem, as I\'ve \"night\", \"light\" and \"bright\" used 2x each within the first stanza. Giving variety expands the description and depth of your message. It also adds creativity and character to the piece. Challenge yourself to see what other words can rhyme!\r\n\r\nKeep at it!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 15:25:32','2025-10-08 15:25:32'),(19635,'judge-event-evaluation-24416-1759902659',24416,464,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,8183,1009,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,60.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Maximillian,\r\n\r\nI can see you are describing love in so many ways and contexts - great work!\r\n\r\nFor the category of poetry, it\'s important to learn and apply the fundamental traits of poetry, including rhyme and rhythm, and the uses of imagery, figure of speech and creative description. The aim is to express a topic in new ways  beyond stating what they are.\r\n\r\nWith your zeal and faith in the Lord that\'s evident in your writing, I encourage you to see how you can express that more creatively.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 15:50:59','2025-10-08 15:50:59'),(19636,'judge-event-evaluation-24977-1759904070',24977,429,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,7092,394,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,0.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Michelle,\r\nThis poem is so beautiful. I love your second stanza, \"in tired hellos and long goodbyes.\" Your phrasing and word choice captures life so well, all the elements of the mundane, the wonder of nature and cities, relationships, and the challenges that come our way. It\'s a refreshing piece on this topic.\r\n\r\nPoint of deduction as the poem needs to be double spacing as stated in the SC guidelines.\r\n\r\nWell done, keep writing! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 16:14:30','2025-10-17 03:16:56'),(19637,'judge-event-evaluation-24971-1759904293',24971,439,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,7043,4679,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,79.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Pretty,\r\n\r\nBeautiful use of patterns and meter. I can see the pacing is used intentionally, and even matching up the form in the last lines of both stanzas.\r\n\r\nWhile the title and the poem is relevant, I think it\'s a missed opportunity as they don\'t support each other. It would have been better to have echoes somehow described in the piece so it adds value. I would also encourage you to try to describe what your point and message is more creatively, finding more original phrasings.\r\n\r\nGreat work!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 16:18:13','2025-10-08 16:18:13'),(19638,'judge-event-evaluation-25307-1759904678',25307,458,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,9237,4200,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,67.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Renbilia,\r\n\r\nGreat references to Scripture used in your poem!\r\nI would have loved to see how you can describe your topic more creatively. The phrasings used in the first stanza are very commonly found in existing songs and poems, including the Bible itself. We absolutely can use Scripture as the point, but the goal of poetry is to find creative new ways to describe existing topics. \r\n\r\nOne way to start is to avoid using the same words multiple times, especially so closely. \"Land\" and \"promise\" has been used three times, and \"strength/strong\" twice.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 16:24:38','2025-10-08 16:24:38'),(19640,'judge-event-evaluation-26210-1759905141',26210,463,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,8144,5934,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,88.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Sebastian,\r\nI like the fresh references for such a classic topic, using the puzzle analogy and the hide reference.\r\n\r\nI found your use of commas unclear as at times its not grammatically correct nor is it an effective poetic device. It doesn\'t suggest pacing that makes sense (such as the first line). \r\n\r\nI really liked the reference of ninety-nine hides, but I feel like it could\'ve been unpacked more. The placement of it doesn\'t make sense, especially between commas, as it reads like you\'re referring to something called ninety-nine hides. I reckon expanding that into two lines of its own would\'ve given it more character, especially considering you\'re using the analogy of sheep to tie in to the title and theme.\r\n\r\nPoints deducted as the title is misspelled, and the poem needs to be in double spacing as stated in the SC guidelines.\r\n\r\nGreat work stil!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 16:32:21','2025-10-08 16:32:22'),(19641,'judge-event-evaluation-24982-1759905406',24982,429,21,7,3,2025,20,'062',NULL,7093,394,9289,6,NULL,NULL,100,64.00,-10,NULL,'Hi Stephanie,\r\n\r\nBeautiful illustration of His light in your life! \r\n\r\nI encourage you to use different words that rhyme and not have the same words closely or repeated. I can see that \"windows\" are used closely after each other, and \"soul\" rhymed with \"soul\". Considering you are using direct rhymes as your form, then \"alive\" and \"live\" do not rhyme.\r\n\r\nKeep growing on the fundamentals of poetry writing!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-08 16:36:46','2025-10-08 16:36:46'),(19642,'judge-event-evaluation-25343-1759971802',25343,464,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,8189,1009,8535,11,NULL,NULL,100,55.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi, Fiona, you have a good imagination, I wonder what Kirby is doing there, haha ^^ The idea of the scene is cute, and the colors match the calm night theme nicely. To improve, try working more on proportions and cleaner outlines so it looks more polished. Adding shading or background details could also help the picture feel more complete. Keep practicing your shapes and colors, and you\'ll see some improvements :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-09 11:03:22','2025-10-09 11:03:22'),(19643,'judge-event-evaluation-24573-1759972342',24573,430,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,7602,392,8535,11,'Collection',NULL,100,78.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Salvio, I like how you made the buildings, their shading and perspectives are on point, and the plants in the foreground sell your perspective even more. However, it seems that the perspective of the car and the bricks and lines on the pavement are off, and it unfortunately it really impacts how convincing your perspective is. Overall, its a solid effort with good composition and color choices, keep practicing your perspective and you\'ll see big improvements! Good job, Salvio, I hope to see you again next time with an even better artwork :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-09 11:12:22','2025-10-09 11:12:22'),(19644,'judge-event-evaluation-26593-1759972875',26593,463,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,9082,5934,8535,11,'Collection',NULL,100,71.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Richelle, this piece has a bold concept, it feels almost symbolic. The color contrast between the yellow and blue also makes it stand out. To make it look more appealing, try refining the textures and lighting so the elements blend together more naturally. The wings could use a bit more depth or shading to  match the lighting on the mask and background. Overall, it\'s a creative idea, but maybe try involving more of a BIblical Worldview in your next submission, keep practicing and learn more about composition and I hope to see you again next year with an even better artwork :)\r\n\r\nP.S. nice idea combining 2d and 3d, keep exploring and practicing different ways the merge them and blend them more smoothly, there\'s lot of potential you can do with merging 2d and 3d!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-09 11:21:15','2025-10-09 11:21:15'),(19646,'judge-event-evaluation-27640-1759979669',27640,429,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,7501,394,8535,11,'Collection',NULL,100,55.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Mikayla, the colors in your work are very vibrant, it feels bright and full of energy. However, the shapes and lighting seem unclear, you could improve this by planning out the composition first and defining some forms more clearly before adding effects. Keep practicing clarity and structure, it\'ll help your ideas come across much stronger next time :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-09 13:14:29','2025-10-09 13:14:29'),(19647,'judge-event-evaluation-28551-1759980271',28551,461,21,7,3,2025,167,'411',NULL,9141,7991,8535,11,'Collection',NULL,100,76.00,NULL,NULL,'Hi Michelle, I really like the colors in your artwork, the bring a nice calming mood to the scene. However, the clouds shape and shading could use some work to show its perspective and lighting more clearly. Overall you did a good job, I like the idea and composition of your piece. Keep drawing and keep learning, Michelle :)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-09 13:24:31','2025-10-09 13:24:31'),(19656,'judge-event-evaluation-26457-1760097599',26457,433,21,7,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,7993,5317,9151,7,NULL,NULL,100,84.00,-10,NULL,'It\'s simple. yet meaningful story. \r\nRead more English literature or a story. Also, learn about the show-not-tell technique to improve your writing skills. \r\n\r\nAlso, do not write some dialogue in one paragraph. Start a new paragraph when another speaker starts a conversation.\r\n\r\nWell done! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-10 21:59:59','2025-10-10 21:59:59'),(19657,'judge-event-evaluation-26623-1760097976',26623,446,21,7,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,9060,2276,9151,7,NULL,NULL,100,74.00,-10,NULL,'The introduction of the character should be written as an orientation (beginning). For example, Lyra was an ordinary mermaid who was always unlucky.  \r\nIt was forced to be finished.\r\nSuggestion: Add some explanation of what happened to the other character once she was healed. \r\n\r\nThere were some structural and punctuation errors. Also, do not write some dialogue in one paragraph. Start a new paragraph when another speaker starts a conversation.\r\nGood job! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-10 22:06:16','2025-10-10 22:06:16'),(19658,'judge-event-evaluation-26026-1760098788',26026,463,21,7,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,8082,5934,9151,7,NULL,NULL,100,82.00,-10,NULL,'Question: So, Mr. Richard sued Haven Paws because of its unsanitary and unsafe conditions or overpopulation? (This specific part was confusing)\r\nIn the courtroom, wasn\'t the evidence presented first to the judge? \r\nIt\'s a good idea to choose a courtroom as a setting. But. it would be even better if you learn how the courtroom works. \r\nIt would be better also if you add some sensory details in your writing (the show-not-tell technique). \r\n\r\nIt\'s a good story.   \r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-10 22:19:48','2025-10-10 22:19:48'),(19660,'judge-event-evaluation-26072-1760106509',26072,461,21,7,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,9131,7991,9151,7,NULL,NULL,100,69.00,-10,-1.00,'It\'s a good story. \r\nRead more English stories or texts.\r\nKeep practicing how to build a story through an interesting orientation, a clear complication, and then close with a strong re-orientation.  \r\nLearn more about sensory detail, the show-not-tell technique. \r\n\r\nYou have potential. ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 00:28:29','2025-10-11 00:28:29'),(19661,'judge-event-evaluation-24571-1760164308',24571,430,21,7,3,2025,22,'064',NULL,7616,392,9291,8,NULL,NULL,100,0.00,-10,0.00,'This is a beautifully written book report. The subject matter of such a complex and spiritual book was handled meaningfully and with clear authenticity and conviction. You have presented Tozer\'s message and your own personal reflections with maturity and eloquence. Your obvious passion to pursue God as articulated so beautifully in your reflections brought me to tears! Well done! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 16:31:48','2025-10-17 03:07:25'),(19662,'judge-event-evaluation-26030-1760166740',26030,463,21,7,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,8084,5934,9151,7,NULL,NULL,100,73.00,-10,NULL,'Just write each dialogue in normal form and font; you don\'t have to italicize those parts.  \r\nStart a new paragraph for a different speaker. \r\nUnless it\'s a chat form like Instagram DM or WhatsApp. \r\nLearn more about the dialog tag and how to use a dash or an em dash (punctuation) \r\n\r\nThe story was good. Please explain more about the bullying situation that Venus had to deal with. It would build the whole story more meaningful. ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 17:12:20','2025-10-11 17:12:20'),(19663,'judge-event-evaluation-26225-1760167202',26225,461,21,7,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,9194,7991,9151,7,NULL,NULL,100,74.00,-10,NULL,'It\'s a simple, yet good story. \r\n\r\nSuggestion: Add a conflict that both of them had to deal with. For example, the bicycle was really stolen. So, Ace had to be accountable for it. It would make the story more interesting. \r\n\r\nPractice more. You have potential. ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 17:20:02','2025-10-11 17:20:02'),(19664,'judge-event-evaluation-25537-1760167940',25537,429,21,7,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,7490,394,9151,7,NULL,NULL,100,65.00,-10,-2.00,'So, what is the conflict? Was it because they approached the hungry man in different ways?\r\nDoes the \'wall\' in paragraph 5 refer to a concrete matter or a poetic meaning?\r\nThen, what happened with the hungry man in the end? Did he survive, or become better?\r\n\r\nDevelop the story further with an interesting orientation, to a clear conflict, then finish with strong ending.  \r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 17:32:20','2025-10-11 17:32:20'),(19665,'judge-event-evaluation-26275-1760168631',26275,463,21,7,3,2025,22,'064',NULL,8158,5934,9291,8,NULL,NULL,100,0.00,-10,NULL,'This book report navigated the plot of the book really well, along with expressing your own personal reflections on the story. There were some good links to Biblical principles. More Biblical references or links between the message of the Gospel and salvation through Jesus Christ could have been portrayed to support the claims stated in the conclusion. Well done! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 17:43:51','2025-10-17 03:52:02'),(19667,'judge-event-evaluation-24568-1760169008',24568,430,21,7,3,2025,22,'064',NULL,7617,392,9291,8,NULL,NULL,100,0.00,-10,NULL,'Really well written book report dealing with both intellectual and spiritual matter. You have explained the claims and convictions of the author articulately, while incorporating Biblical values. However, as you had a some word count to spare, it would have been great to hear more of your own personal thoughts and reflections on the subject!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 17:50:08','2025-10-17 03:03:36'),(19670,'judge-event-evaluation-23892-1760170047',23892,447,21,7,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,9067,6328,9151,7,NULL,NULL,100,85.00,-10,NULL,'It\'s amazing writing. Not everybody could write in the old English version. \r\n\r\nWho was Jesse Sarynx? You didn\'t explain more about this character. Also, did Michael come back to his house?\r\n\r\nStart a new paragraph when another speaker starts a conversation. Do not combine in one paragraph. ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 18:07:27','2025-10-11 18:07:27'),(19671,'judge-event-evaluation-25305-1760170131',25305,458,21,7,3,2025,22,'064',NULL,9236,4200,9291,8,NULL,NULL,100,0.00,-10,0.00,'Interesting book report! You covered the plot of the story well with some good links to Scripture with references well used. However, a deeper focus on Biblical principles could have been used. Overall, well done! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 18:08:51','2025-10-16 17:30:30'),(19672,'judge-event-evaluation-24570-1760170313',24570,430,21,7,3,2025,22,'064',NULL,7619,392,9291,8,NULL,NULL,100,0.00,-10,-4.00,'Great book report covering both a clear description of the plot and reflection on the deeper Biblical principles behind the story. Word count should have been included as it was unfortunately over by 100+ words, and spacing before the conclusion was incorrect. More links to Scripture, particularly in the conclusion, could have been added. Overall, well done! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 18:11:53','2025-10-17 03:04:03'),(19673,'judge-event-evaluation-25304-1760170805',25304,458,21,7,3,2025,22,'064',NULL,9234,4200,9291,8,NULL,NULL,100,0.00,-10,NULL,'Interesting book report! You described the storyline well, however, it seemed to be more of a retelling of the story, rather than an evaluation of the book. Some references to Biblical principles were present but could have been more clearly linked to the plot. Unfortunately, some paragraphs appeared to retell the same content. Some more personal reflections on the message of the book would have been good. Overall, well done! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 18:20:05','2025-10-16 17:29:11'),(19676,'judge-event-evaluation-25303-1760171258',25303,458,21,7,3,2025,22,'064',NULL,7421,4200,9291,8,NULL,NULL,100,0.00,-10,-1.00,'Interesting book report! Clear description of the plot was given. However, it appeared to be more of a retelling of the story, rather than an evaluation of the book. Some references to Scripture and Biblical principles were included. There was a short analysis of one character, Edmund, and the redemptive themes of his story. However, further exploration into the links between salvation through Jesus Christ could have been included. Unfortunately, no word count was included. Overall, well done!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 18:27:38','2025-10-17 03:24:58'),(19677,'judge-event-evaluation-25312-1760171318',25312,458,21,7,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,7423,4200,9151,7,NULL,NULL,100,77.00,-10,NULL,'Do not use other color in the whole story. Was the yellow part an error or intentional? \r\nUse one font only. \r\nAvoid some bold words. \r\nThere were some structural and punctuation errors. Also, do not write some dialogue in one paragraph. Start a new paragraph when another speaker starts a conversation.\r\n\r\nEven though the theme you chose was amazing, its appearance reduced the overall value. ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 18:28:38','2025-10-11 18:28:38'),(19679,'judge-event-evaluation-26975-1760171392',26975,473,21,7,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,7932,3716,9151,7,NULL,NULL,100,85.00,-10,NULL,'There were some structural and punctuation errors. Also, do not write some dialogue in one paragraph. Start a new paragraph when another speaker starts a conversation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 18:29:52','2025-10-11 18:29:52'),(19680,'judge-event-evaluation-28655-1760171458',28655,458,21,7,3,2025,22,'064',NULL,7381,4200,9291,8,NULL,NULL,0,0.00,NULL,NULL,'Did not attend',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 18:30:58','2025-10-15 18:18:34'),(19681,'judge-event-evaluation-28546-1760171707',28546,456,21,7,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,9125,4927,9151,7,NULL,NULL,100,74.00,-10,NULL,'It\'s a simple yet good story. \r\nThe appearance is also important, such as vocabulary, structure, and neatness. ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 18:35:07','2025-10-11 18:35:07'),(19683,'judge-event-evaluation-26045-1760172065',26045,461,21,7,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,8293,7991,9151,7,NULL,NULL,100,81.00,-10,NULL,'Don\'t use the word \'depression\' in your story. It\'s better to show it through character reaction. Also, show it by using sensory details and the show-not-tell technique. \r\n\r\nWhat does it mean \'... ends at 27 with the balance life I dreamed of.\"? Did she die?',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 18:41:05','2025-10-11 18:41:05'),(19684,'judge-event-evaluation-26539-1760172123',26539,461,21,7,3,2025,21,'063',NULL,8303,7991,9291,7,NULL,NULL,100,78.00,-10,NULL,'Interesting story based on a very complex topic. Well written and very creative. Some more clear links to Biblical truth could have been included to support resolution. Overall, well done! ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 18:42:03','2025-10-11 18:42:03'),(19685,'judge-event-evaluation-25129-1760172135',25129,429,21,7,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,7499,394,9151,7,NULL,NULL,100,72.00,-10,NULL,'You already introduced the character\'s name, so don\'t put a quotation mark for a name. Just capitalize. Learn more about how to use quotation marks in a story/ text. \r\n\r\nStart a new paragraph when another speaker starts a conversation. Always check punctuation and tenses.  \r\n\r\nDid Dallan suddenly see, or stay blind while fighting with the King? Because you didn\'t show any explanation of how the Thing directed Dallan about the stone\'s position or the King. \r\nSo, what exactly was \'the ultimate treasure\'?\r\n\r\nThere were too many parts that were forced to be completed. It\'s better if you cut some parts and develop more in certain areas. Two areas were enough for a blind person. Or, develop more on the fighting with the King rather than many fights with others. ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 18:42:15','2025-10-11 18:42:16'),(19686,'judge-event-evaluation-28662-1760172144',28662,458,21,7,3,2025,21,'063',NULL,7384,4200,9291,7,NULL,NULL,0,0.00,NULL,NULL,'Did not attend',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 18:42:24','2025-10-11 18:42:24'),(19688,'judge-event-evaluation-26273-1760172664',26273,463,21,7,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,9087,5934,9151,7,NULL,NULL,100,70.00,-10,NULL,'For reference, a short story only focuses on one main character. Who was the main character in your story-Arabelle, Sammuel, or the teacher? In addition, choose one specific conflict only. There were too many conflicts in your short story. \r\n\r\nAvoid using this sign \'?!\'. \r\nDo not use ellipses (...) too many times. It\'s better if you explain with some dialogue tags. \r\nAlso, do not write some dialogue in one paragraph. Start a new paragraph when another speaker starts a conversation.\r\n',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 18:51:04','2025-10-11 18:51:04'),(19690,'judge-event-evaluation-26604-1760173389',26604,446,21,7,3,2025,7,'013',NULL,9058,2276,9151,7,NULL,NULL,100,72.00,-10,NULL,'There were some structural and punctuation errors. Also, do not write some dialogue in one paragraph. Start a new paragraph when another speaker starts a conversation.\r\nIn paragraph 4, instead of writing as reported speech, it\'s better to write as a conversation between two characters. ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-11 19:03:09','2025-10-11 19:03:09'),(19692,'judge-event-evaluation-25657-1760173470',25657,461,21,7,3,2025,21,'063',NULL,9183,7991,9291,7,NULL,NULL,100,68.00,-10,-1.00,'Very creative story! Unfortunately word count was missing. \r\nInteresting characters and theme. A more clear plot development could have been included. 